## Creating and managing mailing lists [/Mailing Lists/lists/create.{Format}{?apikey}]

### Creating a mailing list [POST /lists/create.{Format}{?apikey}]
Creates a new empty mailing list in your account.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.

        
+ Request (application/json)


    + `Name` : The name of the new mailing list. ***(Required)***
    + `ConfirmationPage` : The URL of the page that will be displayed at the end of the subscription process. ***(Optional)***
    + `RedirectAfterUnsubscribePage` : The URL of the page that users will be redirected after unsubscribing from your mailing list. ***(Optional)***

 
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
        
        
    + Body
        
            {
                "Name":"New List",
                "ConfirmationPage":"www.someUrl.com",
                "RedirectAfterUnsubscribePage":"www.someUrl.com"
            }
  
+ Response 200 (application/json)


    
    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful. 
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful. 
    + `Context` : The unique id for the mailing list created. 
        
    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": "6ca52d31-765c-4760-a78e-91e511e49d76"
            }

### Updating a mailing list [POST /lists/{MailingListID}/update.{Format}{?apikey}]
Updates the properties of an existing mailing list.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string)
     The ID of the mailing list to be updated. 
 
        
+ Request (application/json)

    + `Name` :  The name of the updated mailing list. ***(Required)***
    + `ConfirmationPage` :  The URL of the page that will be displayed at the end of the subscription process. ***(Optional)***
    + `RedirectAfterUnsubscribePage` :  The URL of the page that users will be redirected after unsubscribing from your mailing list. ***(Optional)***


    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
            
    + Body
    
            {
                "Name":"New List Name",
                "ConfirmationPage":"www.someotherUrl.com",
                "RedirectAfterUnsubscribePage":"www.someotherUrl.com"
            }
        

+ Response 200 (application/json)



    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful. 
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful. 
    + `Context` : The unique id for the updated mailing list. 

    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": "e5f6c0a3-1fe6-4d89-951e-eafae0b01368"
            }
    
### Deleting a mailing list [DELETE /lists/{MailingListID}/delete.{Format}{?apikey}]
Deletes a mailing list from your account.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + MailingListID: `b9c67cb4-a821-4187-930d-79d81a3067df` (required, string)
    The ID of the mailing list to be deleted.


+ Response 200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful. 
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful. 
    + `Context` : Context will be null if successful. 
    
    + Body 
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": null
            }

### Creating a custom field [POST /lists/{MailingListID}/customfields/create.{Format}{?apikey}]
Creates a new custom field in the specified mailing list.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string)
    The ID of the mailing list where the custom field will belong.

        
+ Request (application/json)


    + `Name` : The name of the custom field. ***(Required)***
    + `CustomFieldType` : Specifies the data type of the custom field. This must be one of the following values. ***(Optional)*** <br/> If omitted, Text will be assumed.
        - `Text` : To accept any text as input.
        - `Number` : To accept only numeric values as input.
        - `DateTime` : To accept only date values as input, with or without time.
        - `SingleSelectDropdown` : To accept only values explicitly defined in a list.
        - `CheckBox` : To accept only values of true or false.

    + `Options` : If you want to create a custom field of type SingleSelectDropdown, you must set this parameter to specify the available options for the user to choose from. Use a comma (,) to separate different options. ***(Optional)***
    + `IsRequired` : Specify whether this field will be mandatory on not, when a subscriber is added to your list by any means. You should specify a value of either true or false. If omitted, false will be assumed. ***(Optional)***
    + `IsHidden` : Specify whether this field will be visible by your subscribers on not, in their update profile page. If omitted, false will be assumed. ***(Optional)***


    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
        
    + Body
        
            {
                "Name": "Town",
                "CustomFieldType":"SingleSelectDropdown",
                "Options":"Athens,London,New York"
            }

+ Response 200 (application/json)



    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful. 
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful. 
    + `Context` : The unique id for the new custom field. 
            
            
    + Body
        
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": "b42b4e0f-ca2f-403d-8231-32a2405651af"
            }

### Updating a custom field [POST /lists/{MailingListID}/customfields/{CustomFieldID}/update.{Format}{?apikey}]
Updates the properties of an existing custom field in the specified mailing list.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + CustomFieldID: `b42b4e0f-ca2f-403d-8231-32a2405651af` (required, string)
    The ID of the custom field to be updated.
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string)
    The ID of the mailing list where the custom field belongs.

        
+ Request (application/json)


    + `Name` : The name of the custom field. ***(Required)***
    + `CustomFieldType` : Specifies the data type of the custom field. This must be one of the following values.  ***(Optional)***<br/> If omitted, Text will be assumed.
        - `Text` : To accept any text as input.
        - `Number` : To accept only numeric values as input.
        - `DateTime` : To accept only date values as input, with or without time.
        - `SingleSelectDropdown` : To accept only values explicitly defined in a list.
        - `CheckBox` : To accept only values of true or false.

    + `Options` : If you want to create a custom field of type SingleSelectDropdown, you must set this parameter to specify the available options for the user to choose from. Use a comma (,) to separate different options. ***(Optional)***
    + `IsRequired` : Specify whether this field will be mandatory on not, when a subscriber is added to your list by any means. You should specify a value of either true or false. If omitted, false will be assumed. ***(Optional)***
    + `IsHidden` : Specify whether this field will be visible by your subscribers on not, in their update profile page. If omitted, false will be assumed. ***(Optional)***


    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
            
        
    + Body
        
            {
                "Name": "City",
                "CustomFieldType":"SingleSelectDropdown",
                "Options":"Frankfurt,London,Paris,Rome"
            }

+ Response 200 (application/json)
        
      
        
    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful. 
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful. 
    + `Context` : The unique id for the updated custom field. 
    
    
    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": null
            }
           

### Removing a custom field [DELETE /lists/{MailingListID}/customfields/{CustomFieldID}/delete.{Format}{?apikey}]
Removes a custom field definition from the specified mailing list.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + CustomFieldID: `b42b4e0f-ca2f-403d-8231-32a2405651af` (required, string)
    The ID of the custom field to be deleted.
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string)
    The ID of the mailing list where the custom field belongs.
    
    
+ Response 200 (application/json)
    
    
    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful. 
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful. 
    + `Context` : Context will be null if successful. 


    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
            
    + Body 
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": null
            }


# Group Subscribers

## Subscribers
Through the Moosend Subscriber API you can add or remove mailing list subscribers, fetch and update their information and batch import new subscribers. 


## Getting subscribers [/Mailing Lists/subscribers/{Status}.{Format}{?apikey}{?Page}{?PageSize}]

### Getting subscribers [GET /lists/{MailingListID}/subscribers/{Status}.{Format}{?apikey}{?Page}{?PageSize}]
Gets a list of all subscribers in a given mailing list. You may filter the list by setting a date to fetch those subscribed since then and/or by their status. Because the results for this call could be quite big, paging information is required as input.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)

        + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string)
    The ID of the mailing list where the subscribers belong.
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + Status: `Subscribed` (required, string)
    Specifies what type of subscriber statistics results will be returned.
    
        + Members
            + Subscribed
            + Unsubscribed
            + Bounced
            + Removed
            
    + Page: `1` (optional, number)
    Specifies the page of subscriber statistics results will be returned.
    + PageSize: `100` (optional, number)
    Specifies the page size of subscriber statistics results will be returned.

    
+ Response 200 (application/json)

  
  
    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : The response context. This contains all the following information for the subscribers of requested mailing list:
    + `Paging` : A list with all the following paging information.
        - `PageSize` : The page size of the results. This will be 0 if not defined.
        - `CurrentPage` : The number of the result page. This will be 1 if not defined.
        - `Totalresults` : The number of all the mailing lists that are included in the response.
        - `TotalPageCount` : The number of all the available mailing list pages for your account.
        - `SortExpression` : The sort expression associated with the column or columns being sorted.
        - `SortIsAscending` : This will be false if the results are not displayed with an ascending order based on the sort expression.
    + `Subscribers` : A list with all the subscribers for the requested mailing list, with all the following information:
        - `ID` : The id of the subscriber.
        - `Name` : The name of the subscriber.
        - `Email` : The email of the subscriber.
        - `CreatedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was added to the requested mailing list.
        - `UnsubscribedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was unsubscribed from the requested mailing list. This will be null if not unsubscribed.
        - `UnsubscribedFromID` : The 
        - `SubscribeType` : The status of the subscriber. It can be one of the following:
            - `1` : Subscribed.
            - `2` : Unsubscribed.
            - `3` : Bounced.
            - `4` : Removed.
        - `SubscribeMethod` : The method from which the member was subscribed to the mailing list. 
            - `0` : For subscription form. 
            - `1` : For file import. 
            - `2` : For manually added.
    + `CustomFields` : A list with all the custom fields for the requested mailing list.
        - `CustomFieldID` : The id of the custom field.
        - `Name` : The name of the custom field.
        - `Value` : The value defined for each email for the specific custom field.


    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
            
    
    + Body 
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": {
                "Paging": {
                  "PageSize": 500,
                  "CurrentPage": 1,
                  "TotalResults": 2,
                  "TotalPageCount": 1,
                  "SortExpression": "CreatedOn",
                  "SortIsAscending": false
                },
                "Subscribers": [
                  {
                    "ID": "4d03536e-7263-4a45-add0-8fe9568d7481",
                    "Name": "Maria",
                    "Email": "maria@email.com",
                    "CreatedOn": "/Date(1456236266953+0000)/",
                    "UpdatedOn": "/Date(1465286948363+0100)/",
                    "UnsubscribedOn": null,
                    "UnsubscribedFromID": null,
                    "SubscribeType": 1,
                    "SubscribeMethod": 2,
                    "CustomFields": [
                      {
                        "CustomFieldID": "dbc599a6-3ac0-4843-830c-31fa78699fcc",
                        "Name" : "ID",
                        "Value": "1233"
                      },
                      {
                        "CustomFieldID": "bfe484f1-030f-4f8d-bdfa-93abc3b227c0",
                        "Name" : "City",
                        "Value": "Athens"
                      }
                    ],
                    "RemovedOn": null
                  },
                  {
                    "ID": "83485f6c-569c-4012-ab2e-f91d3f888995",
                    "Name": "Andreas",
                    "Email": "andreas@moosend.com",
                    "CreatedOn": "/Date(1454421397847+0000)/",
                    "UpdatedOn": "/Date(1465286972657+0100)/",
                    "UnsubscribedOn": null,
                    "UnsubscribedFromID": null,
                    "SubscribeType": 1,
                    "SubscribeMethod": 2,
                    "CustomFields": [
                      {
                        "CustomFieldID": "dbc599a6-3ac0-4843-830c-31fa78699fcc",
                        "Name" : "ID",
                        "Value": "1333"
                      },
                      {
                        "CustomFieldID": "bfe484f1-030f-4f8d-bdfa-93abc3b227c0",
                        "Name" : "City",
                        "Value": "Liverpool"
                      }
                    ],
                    "RemovedOn": null
                  }
                ]
              }
            }    
   
      

## Get subscriber details [/subscribers/{MailingListID}/view.{Format}{?apikey}{?Email}]

### Get subscriber by email address [GET /subscribers/{MailingListID}/view.{Format}{?apikey}{?Email}]
Searches for a subscriber with the specified email address in the specified mailing list and returns detailed information such as id, name, date created, date unsubscribed, status and custom fields

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string)
    The ID of the mailing list where the subscriber belongs.
    + Email: someEmail@email.com (required, string)
    The email of the subscriber.
    
+ Response 200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : The response context. Contains all the following information for the requested subscriber:
        - `ID` : The id of the subscriber.
        - `Name` : The name of the subscriber.
        - `Email` : The email of the subscriber.
        - `CreatedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was added to the given mailing list.
        - `UnsubscribedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was unsubscribed from the given mailing list. This will be null if not unsubscribed.
        - `UnsubscribedFromID` : The id that the subscriber is unsubscribed from.
        - `SubscribeType` : The status of the subscriber. It can be one of the following:
            - `1` : Subscribed.
            - `2` : Unsubscribed.
            - `3` : Bounced.
            - `4` : Removed.
        - `SubscribeMethod` : The method from which the member was subscribed to the mailing list. 
            - `0` : For subscription form. 
            - `1` : For file import.
            - `2` : For manually added.
        - `CustomFields` : A list with all the custom fields for the requested subscriber. Each custom field contains the following:
            - `CustomFieldID` : The id of the custom field.
            - `Name` : The name of the custom field.
            - `Value` : The value defined for the specific custom field.
        - `RemovedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was removed from the given mailing list.


    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
            
    + Body 
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": {
                "ID": "9bef1735-f04d-4472-b029-68eb7fa2cfe7",
                "Name": "Andreas",
                "Email": "andreas@moosend.com",
                "CreatedOn": "/Date(1461777152597+0100)/",
                "UpdatedOn": "/Date(1461777152597+0100)/",
                "UnsubscribedOn": null,
                "UnsubscribedFromID": null,
                "SubscribeType": 1,
                "SubscribeMethod": 2,
                "CustomFields": [
                  {
                    "CustomFieldID": "b7e68e81-b6ab-4caa-8d13-e65871b32386",
                    "Name": "Registered",
                    "Value": "4/21/2016 12:00:00 AM"
                  },
                  {
                    "CustomFieldID": "9df6dcc4-bef2-47e7-93af-86889b6b6d6a",
                    "Name": "Age",
                    "Value": "24"
                  },
                  {
                    "CustomFieldID": "0d2199aa-65fc-448c-b9fe-199e3b72ebc5",
                    "Name": "Some custom field",
                    "Value": "Something"
                  },
                  {
                    "CustomFieldID": "46721a6b-09aa-46ff-bab1-a0b75dea24cf",
                    "Name": "Some custom field",
                    "Value": "Text1"
                  }
                ],
                "RemovedOn": null
              }
            }

### Get subscriber by id [GET  /subscribers/{MailingListID}/find/{SubscriberID}.{Format}{?apikey}]
Searches for a subscriber with the specified unique id in the specified mailing list and returns detailed information such as email, name, date created, date unsubscribed, status and custom fields.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string) 
    The ID of the mailing list to search the subscriber in. 
    + SubscriberID: `118e41dc-bb9e-435d-a86a-e5bd374668a8` (required, string)
    The id of the subscriber being searched.
    

+ Response 200 (application/json)



    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : The response context. Contains all the following information for the requested subscriber:
        - `ID` : The id of the subscriber.
        - `Name` : The name of the subscriber.
        - `Email` : The email of the subscriber.
        - `CreatedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was added to the given mailing list.
        - `UnsubscribedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was unsubscribed from the given mailing list. This will be null if not unsubscribed.
        - `UnsubscribedFromID` : The id that the subscriber is unsubscribed from.
        - `SubscribeType` : The status of the subscriber. It can be one of the following:
            - `1` : Subscribed.
            - `2` : Unsubscribed.
            - `3` : Bounced.
            - `4` : Removed.
        - `SubscribeMethod` : The method from which the member was subscribed to the mailing list. 
            - `0` : For subscription form. 
            - `1` : For file import.
            - `2`:  For manually added.
        - `CustomFields` : A list with all the custom fields for the requested subscriber. Each custom field contains the following:
            - `CustomFieldID` : The id of the custom field.
            - `Name` : The name of the custom field.
            - `Value` : The value defined for the specific custom field.
        - `RemovedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was removed from the given mailing list.
        

    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
            
    + Body 
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": {
                "ID": "118e41dc-bb9e-435d-a86a-e5bd374668a8",
                "Name": "Some name",
                "Email": "getmoocampaigns+1@gmail.com",
                "CreatedOn": "/Date(1464952683773+0100)/",
                "UpdatedOn": "/Date(1465380328390+0100)/",
                "UnsubscribedOn": null,
                "UnsubscribedFromID": null,
                "SubscribeType": 4,
                "SubscribeMethod": 2,
                "CustomFields": [],
                "RemovedOn": "/Date(1465381597743+0100)/"
              }
            }

          
## Add or update subscribers [/subscribers/{MailingListID}/subscribe.{Format}{?apikey}]

### Adding subscribers [POST /subscribers/{MailingListID}/subscribe.{Format}{?apikey}]
Adds a new subscriber to the specified mailing list. If there is already a subscriber with the specified email address in the list, an update will be performed instead. The rate limit for this request is 10 requests per 10 seconds (*per API key).

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string)
    The ID of the mailing list to add the new member.
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    

        
+ Request (application/json)


    + `Name` : The name of the member. ***(Optional)***
    + `Email` : The email address of the member. ***(Required)***
    + `HasExternalDoubleOptIn`: When true, flags the added member as having given their subscription consent by other means. ***(Optional)***
    + `CustomFields` : A list of name-value pairs that match the member's custom fields defined in the mailing list. ***(Optional)***
    <br/>For example, if you have two custom fields named Age and Country, you should specify values for them as following example.


    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
            
    + Body
    
            {
                "Name" : "Paul",
                "Email" : "someEmail@email.com",
                "HasExternalDoubleOptIn": false,
                "CustomFields": [
                    "Age=25",
                    "Country=USA"
                ]
            }
     
+ Response 200 (application/json)



    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : The response context. Contains all the following information for the requested subscriber:
        - `ID` : The id of the subscriber.
        - `Name` : The name of the subscriber.
        - `Email` : The email of the subscriber.
        - `CreatedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was added to the given mailing list.
        - `UnsubscribedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was unsubscribed from the given mailing list. This will be null if not unsubscribed.
        - `UnsubscribedFromID` : The id that the subscriber is unsubscribed from.
        - `SubscribeType` : The status of the subscriber. It can be one of the following:
            - `1` : Subscribed.
            - `2` : Unsubscribed.
            - `3` : Bounced.
            - `4` : Removed.
        - `SubscribeMethod` : The method from which the member was subscribed to the mailing list. 
            - `0` : For subscription form. 
            - `1` : For file import.
            - `2`:  For manually added.
        - `CustomFields` : A list with all the custom fields for the requested subscriber. Each custom field contains the following:
            - `CustomFieldID` : The id of the custom field.
            - `Name` : The name of the custom field.
            - `Value` : The value defined for the specific custom field.
        - `RemovedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was removed from the given mailing list.

    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": {
                "ID": "f582c388-7916-4890-a9ab-b592615ef095",
                "Name": "Paul",
                "Email": "someemail@email.com",
                "CreatedOn": "/Date(1465379934028)/",
                "UpdatedOn": "/Date(1465379934028)/",
                "UnsubscribedOn": null,
                "UnsubscribedFromID": null,
                "SubscribeType": 1,
                "SubscribeMethod": 2,
                 "CustomFields": [
                  {
                    "CustomFieldID": "728f6774-37ea-4d81-8607-ce8308136760",
                    "Name": "Age",
                    "Value": "25"
                  },
                  {
                    "CustomFieldID": "b6380e04-c3a6-425b-9931-d25897fa4752",
                    "Name": "Country",
                    "Value": "USA"
                  }
                ],
                "RemovedOn": null
              }
            }
            
### Adding multiple subscribers [POST /subscribers/{MailingListID}/subscribe_many.{Format}{?apikey}]
This method allows you to add multiple subscribers in a mailing list with a single call. If some subscribers already exist with the given email addresses, they will be updated. If you try to add a subscriber with an invalid email address, this attempt will be ignored, as the process will skip to the next subscriber automatically. The rate limit for this request is 2 requests per 10 seconds (*per API key). 
 
+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string) 
    The ID of the mailing list to add subscribers to.        


        
+ Request (application/json)

    + `HasExternalDoubleOptIn`: When true, flags the added members as having given their subscription consent by other means. ***(Optional)***
    + `Subscribers` : A list of up to 1000 subscribers to add to the mailing list. You may specify the email address, the name and the custom fields for each subscriber. ***(Required)***
    <br/>The following example demonstrates the format each subscriber should be written in your request, assuming that you also have two custom fields named Age and Country. 
       
       
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
        
    + Body
    
            {  
                "HasExternalDoubleOptIn": false,
                "Subscribers":[  
                  {  
                     "Name":"test1Email",
                     "Email":"test1@test.com",
                     "CustomFields":[  
                        "Country=UK"
                     ]
                  },
                  {  
                     "Name":"test2133Email",
                     "Email":"test2133@test.com",
                     "CustomFields":[  
                        "Age=25",
                        "Country=USA"
                     ]
                  }
               ]
            }


+ Response  200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error message will show how many and which emails are invalid. It will be null if all emails are valid.
    + `Context` : A list with response contexts. Each context contains all the following information for each subscriber:
        - `ID` : The id of the subscriber.
        - `Name` : The name of the subscriber.
        - `Email` : The email of the subscriber.
        - `CreatedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was added to the given mailing list.
        - `UnsubscribedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was unsubscribed from the given mailing list. This will be null if not unsubscribed.
        - `UnsubscribedFromID` : The id that the subscriber is unsubscribed from.
        - `SubscribeType` : The status of the subscriber. It can be one of the following:
            - `1` : Subscribed.
            - `2` : Unsubscribed.
            - `3` : Bounced.
            - `4` : Removed.
        - `SubscribeMethod` : The method from which the member was subscribed to the mailing list. 
            - `0` : For subscription form. 
            - `1` : For file import.
            - `2`:  For manually added.
        - `CustomFields` : A list with all the custom fields for the requested subscriber. Each custom field contains the following:
            - `CustomFieldID` : The id of the custom field.
            - `Name` : The name of the custom field.
            - `Value` : The value defined for the specific custom field.
        - `RemovedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was removed from the given mailing list.

    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": "2 items with invalid email address were ignored: email@email, email2@email",
              "Context": [
                {
                  "ID": "ca506fc5-0967-4756-8848-74e9766bdbdd",
                  "Name": "test1Email",
                  "Email": "test1@test.com",
                  "CreatedOn": "/Date(1465377493907+0100)/",
                  "UpdatedOn": "/Date(1465381164389)/",
                  "UnsubscribedOn": null,
                  "UnsubscribedFromID": null,
                  "SubscribeType": 1,
                  "SubscribeMethod": 1,
                  "CustomFields": [
                    {
                      "CustomFieldID": "42acf2cf-1096-4c80-960b-051791d9a276",
                      "Name": "Country",
                      "Value": "UK"
                    }
                  ],
                  "RemovedOn": null
                },
                {
                  "ID": "b751f349-f6b3-4b14-8d75-c37dfafbe40a",
                  "Name": "test2133Email",
                  "Email": "test2133@test.com",
                  "CreatedOn": "/Date(1465377493907+0100)/",
                  "UpdatedOn": "/Date(1465381164389)/",
                  "UnsubscribedOn": null,
                  "UnsubscribedFromID": null,
                  "SubscribeType": 1,
                  "SubscribeMethod": 1,
                  "CustomFields": [
                    {
                      "CustomFieldID": "60d4e2b0-e5ae-4737-9ac5-ce071ab346fb",
                      "Name": "Age",
                      "Value": 25
                    },
                    {
                      "CustomFieldID": "42acf2cf-1096-4c80-960b-051791d9a276",
                      "Name": "Country",
                      "Value": "USA"
                    }
                  ],
                  "RemovedOn": null
                }
              ]
            }

### Updating a subscriber [POST  /subscribers/{MailingListID}/update/{SubscriberID}.{Format}{?apikey}]
Updates a subscriber in the specified mailing list. 

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string) 
    The ID of the mailing list that contains the subscriber
    + SubscriberID: `118e41dc-bb9e-435d-a86a-e5bd374668a8` (required, string)
    The id of the subscriber to be updated


        
+ Request (application/json)


    + `Name` : The name of the member. ***(Optional)***
    + `Email` : The email address of the member. ***(Required)***
    + `HasExternalDoubleOptIn`: When true, flags the added member as having given their subscription consent by other means. ***(Optional)***
    + `CustomFields` : A list of name-value pairs that match the member's custom fields defined in the mailing list. ***(Optional)***
    <br/>For example, if you have two custom fields named Age and Country, you should specify values for them as following example.
    
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
        
    + Body
    
            {
                "Name" : "Some Name",
                "HasExternalDoubleOptIn": false,
                "Email" : "someEmail@email.com",
                "CustomFields": [
                    "Age=25",
                    "Country=USA"
                ]
            }
                

+ Response 200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : The response context. Contains all the following information for the requested subscriber:
        - `ID` : The id of the subscriber.
        - `Name` : The name of the subscriber.
        - `Email` : The email of the subscriber.
        - `CreatedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was added to the given mailing list.
        - `UnsubscribedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was unsubscribed from the given mailing list. This will be null if not unsubscribed.
        - `UnsubscribedFromID` : The id that the subscriber is unsubscribed from.
        - `SubscribeType` : The status of the subscriber. It can be one of the following:
            - `1` : Subscribed.
            - `2` : Unsubscribed.
            - `3` : Bounced.
            - `4` : Removed.
        - `SubscribeMethod` : The method from which the member was subscribed to the mailing list. 
            - `0` : For subscription form. 
            - `1` : For file import.
            - `2`:  For manually added.
        - `CustomFields` : A list with all the custom fields for the requested subscriber. Each custom field contains the following:
            - `CustomFieldID` : The id of the custom field.
            - `Name` : The name of the custom field.
            - `Value` : The value defined for the specific custom field.
        - `RemovedOn` : The date time on which the subscriber was removed from the given mailing list.
        
    + Body 
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": {
                "ID": "d75fca65-a2bc-4474-bd4d-307f9cf63a57",
                "Name": "Some name",
                "Email": "someEmail@email.com",
                "CreatedOn": "/Date(1465380655880+0100)/",
                "UpdatedOn": "/Date(1465388373874)/",
                "UnsubscribedOn": null,
                "UnsubscribedFromID": null,
                "SubscribeType": 1,
                "SubscribeMethod": 2,
                "CustomFields": [
                  {
                    "CustomFieldID": "b9a6cb39-ec8f-4e5e-a41a-b64b9b3fc190",
                    "Name" : "Age",
                    "Value": 25
                  },
                  {
                    "CustomFieldID": "1c4ff8dc-48e3-4af1-ae4f-2b1b81a44d17",
                    "Name": "Country",
                    "Value": "USA"
                  }
                ],
                "RemovedOn": null
              }
            }

## Remove or Unsubscribe subscribers [/subscribers/unsubscribe.{Format}{?apikey}]

### Unsubscribing subscribers from account [POST  /subscribers/unsubscribe.{Format}{?apikey}]
Unsubscribes a subscriber from the account. The rate limit for this request is 20 requests per 10 seconds (*per API key).  

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.

        
+ Request (application/json)


    + `Email` : The email address of the member. ***(Required)***
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
    
            {
                "Email":"test1@test.com"
            }

+ Response 200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response message for this call. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : The response context for this call. This will be null if successful.

    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": null
            }

### Unsubscribing subscribers from mailing list [POST /subscribers/{MailingListID}/unsubscribe.{Format}{?apikey}]
Unsubscribes a subscriber from the specified mailing list. The rate limit for this request is 20 requests per 10 seconds (*per API key). 

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string) 
    The ID of the mailing list to add subscribers to.  
    
+ Request (application/json)


    + `Email` : The email address of the member. ***(Required)***
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
    
            {
                "Email":"test1@test.com"
            }

+ Response 200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response message for this call. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : The response context for this call. This will be null if successful.

    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": null
            }

### Unsubscribing subscribers from mailing list and a specified campaign [POST /subscribers/{MailingListID}/{CampaignID}/unsubscribe.{Format}{?apikey}]
Unsubscribes a subscriber from the specified mailing list and the specified campaign. 
This call will take into account the setting you have in "unsubscribe settings" and will remove the subscriber from all other mailing lists or not accordingly. The rate limit for this request is 20 requests per 10 seconds (*per API key). 

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + CampaignID: `cbcb297d-52a8-4bed-ae85-640c37c92771` (required, string)
    The ID of the campaign that was sent to the specific mailing list.
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string) 
    The ID of the mailing list to remove the subscriber from.  

    
+ Request (application/json)


    + `Email` : The email address of the member. ***(Required)***
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
    
            {
                "Email":"test1@test.com"
            }

+ Response 200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response message for this call. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : The response context for this call. This will be null if successful.
    
    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": null
            }

### Removing a subscriber [POST /subscribers/{MailingListID}/remove.{Format}{?apikey}]
Removes a subscriber from the specified mailing list permanently (without moving to the suppression list).

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string) 
    The ID of the mailing list to remove the subscriber from.  

    
+ Request (application/json)


    + `Email` : The email address of the member. ***(Required)***
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
    
            {
                "Email":"test1@test.com"
            }

+ Response 200 (application/json)



    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response message for this call. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : The response context for this call. This will be null if successful.
    
    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": null
            }

### Removing multiple subscribers [POST /subscribers/{MailingListID}/remove_many.{Format}{?apikey}]
Removes a list of subscribers from the specified mailing list permanently (without putting them in the suppression list). Any invalid email addresses specified will be ignored.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string) 
    The ID of the mailing list to remove the subscribers from.  

    
+ Request (application/json)


    + `Emails` A list of email addresses to be removed, separated with a comma (,). ***(Required)***
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body

            {  
               "Emails":"someEmail@email.com,someEmail2@email.com,someEmail3@email.com"
            }

+ Response 200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response message for this call. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : The response context for this call. This contains the following:
        - `EmailsIgnored` : The number of the ignored emails.
        - `EmailsProcessed` : The number of the processed emails.

    + Body
    
            {  
               "Code":0,
               "Error":null,
               "Context":{  
                  "EmailsIgnored":0,
                  "EmailsProcessed":3
               }
            }



# Group Campaigns

Through the Campaign API you can create, schedule and send new campaigns, or update information on your draft campaigns. 
It also supports fetching campaign statistics such as the link performance, open / click performance as well as campaign activity by location.

## Getting Campaigns [/campaigns.{Format}{?apikey}]

### Get All Campaigns [GET /campaigns.{Format}{?apikey}]
Returns a list of all campaigns in your account with detailed information. Because the results for this call could be quite big, paging information is required as input.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `bafe55f4-e53e-4651-8164-c6d6ff05081b` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.

+ Response 200 (application/json)



    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful. 
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : Contains all the following information for the new campaign :
        - `Paging` : A list with all the following paging information.
            - `PageSize` : The page size of the results. This will be 0 if not defined.
            - `CurrentPage` : The number of the result page. This will be 1 if not defined.
            - `Totalresults` : The number of all the mailing lists that are included in the response.
            - `TotalPageCount` : The number of all the available mailing list pages for your account.
            - `SortExpression` : The sort expression associated with the column or columns being sorted.
            - `SortIsAscending` : This will be false if the results are not displayed with an ascending order based on the sort expression.
        + `ID` : The id of the cloned campaign. 
        + `Name` : The name of the campaign. 
        + `Subject` : The subject of the campaign.
        + `SiteName` : The site name of the account.
        + `ConfirmationTo` : The email address to which a confirmation message will be sent when the campaign has been successfully sent. 
        + `CreatedOn` : Specifies when the campaign was created.
        + `ABHoursToTest` : Specifies the total number of hours to test version A and B of your campaign before sending the winning version. Will be null if the given campaign is not an A/B split test campaign.
        + `ABCampaignType` : Specifies the type of the A/B split campaign test. It can be one of the following:
            - `0` : For campaign sender test.
            - `1` : For campaign content test.
            - `2` : For subject line test.
        + `ABWinner` : Specifies if the winning campaign is A or B. Will be null if the given campaign is not an A/B split test campaign.
        + `ABWinnerSelectionType` : Specifies the method to determine the winning version for the test. Will be null if the given campaign is not an A/B split test campaign, or one of the following if it is :
            - `0` : If the campaign version with the highest number of unique opens is selected to be sent to the rest of your list.
            - `1` : If the campaign version with the highest number of unique clicks is selected to be sent to the rest of your list.
        + `Status` : The status of the campaign. Will be one of the following:
            - `0` : For Draft.
            - `1` : For Queued for sending.
            - `3` : For Sent.
            - `4` : For Not enough credits.
            - `5` : For Awaiting delivery.
            - `6` : For Sending.
            - `10` : For Deleted.
            - `11` : For Selecting winner.
            - `12` : For Archived.
            - `13` : For Subscription expired.
            - `14` : For Subscription limits exceeded.
        + `DeliveredOn` : The date time that the campaign was delivered. 
        + `ScheduleFor` : The date time that the campaign is scheduled to be delivered.
        + `ScheduledForTimezone` - The selected timezone for the scheduled campaign to be delivered.
        + `MailingLists`: A list that contains the mailing lists selected for this campaign to be sent to.
            - `Campaign` : The campaign associated with this mailing list. This will be null for this case.
            - `MailingList` : Contains the following information for each mailing list:
                - `ID` : The id of the mailing list.
                - `Name` : The name of the mailing list.
                - `ActiveMemberCount` : The number of the active members for this mailing list.
                - `BouncedMemberCount` : The number of the bounced emails for this mailing list.
                - `RemovedMemberCount` : The number of the removed emails for this mailing list.
                - `UnsubscribedMemberCount` : The number of the unsubscribed emails for this mailing list.
                - `Status` : The status of the mailing list. This will be one of the following:
                    - `0` : For created. 
                    - `1` : For imported.
                    - `2` : For importing.
                    - `3` : For deleted.
                - `CustomFieldsDefinition` : The details of the custom fields for the requested mailing list.
                - `CreatedBy`: The ip from where the requested mailing list was created.
                - `CreatedOn` : The date time that the requested mailing list was created.
                - `UpdatedBy` : The ip from where the requested mailing list was updated.
                - `UpdatedOn` : The date time that the requested mailing list was updated.
                - `ImportOperation` : The details of the latest import operation that was performed in the requested mailing list. This will be blank if no import operation was performed for this list.
            - `Segment` : A list with all the following information for the given segment. Will be null if the campaign was not sent to a segment of this mailing list.
                - `ID` : The id of the segment.
                - `Name` : The name of the segment.
                - `MatchType` :  The match criteria selected for this segment. This will be:
                    - `0` : For All.
                    - `1` : For Any.
                - `Criteria` : A list with all the selected criteria for this segment.
                - `CreatedBy`: The ip from where the segment was created.
                - `CreatedOn` : The date time that the segment was created.
                - `UpdatedBy` : The ip from where the segment was updated.
                - `UpdatedOn` : The date time that the segment was updated.
                - `FetchType` : The selected fetch type for the selected segment criteria. This will be:
                    - `0` : For all segment criteria.
                    - `1` : For top segment criteria.
                    - `2` : For top percent segment criteria.
                - `Description` : Contains a string representation of all the selected filters, MatchType criteria and FetchType criteria.
            + `TotalSent` : The number of the total emails sent.
            + `TotalOpens` : The number of the total emails opened.
            + `UniqueOpens` : The number of the total unique emails opened.
            + `TotalBounces` : The number of the total bounce
            + `TotalForwards` : The number of the total forwarded emails. This will count emails forwarded by the "Forward to a friend" personalization tag.
            + `UniqueForwards` : The number of the total unique forwarded emails. This will count emails forwarded by the "Forward to a friend" personalization tag.
            + `TotalLinkClicks` : The number of the total link clicks.
            + `UniqueLinkClicks` : The number of the total unique link clicks.
            + `RecipientsCount` : The number of the total recipients.
            + `IsTransactional` : This value will be false for this case.
            + `TotalComplaints` : The number of the total complaints.
            + `TotalUnsubscribes` : The number of the total unsubscribed emails.
            
        
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
    
            {  
               "Code":0,
               "Error":null,
               "Context":{  
                  "Paging":{  
                     "PageSize":10,
                     "CurrentPage":1,
                     "TotalResults":2,
                     "TotalPageCount":1,
                     "SortExpression":null,
                     "SortIsAscending":true
                  },
                  "Campaigns":[  
                     {  
                        "ID":"cbcb297d-52a8-4bed-ae85-640c37c92771",
                        "Name":"Test Release 1",
                        "Subject":"Test Release 1",
                        "SiteName":"mysite",
                        "ConfirmationTo":"andreas@moosend.com",
                        "CreatedOn":"/Date(1464952661697+0100)/",
                        "ABHoursToTest":null,
                        "ABCampaignType":null,
                        "ABWinner":null,
                        "ABWinnerSelectionType":null,
                        "Status":3,
                        "DeliveredOn":"/Date(1464952817450+0100)/",
                        "ScheduledFor":null,
                        "ScheduledForTimezone":"GTB Standard Time",
                        "MailingLists":[  
                           {  
                              "Campaign":null,
                              "MailingList":{  
                                 "ID":"dce99b7a-2619-4805-aaeb-7fecdcb3c71b",
                                 "Name":"SomeName",
                                 "ActiveMemberCount":0,
                                 "BouncedMemberCount":0,
                                 "RemovedMemberCount":0,
                                 "UnsubscribedMemberCount":0,
                                 "Status":0,
                                 "CustomFieldsDefinition":[  

                                 ],
                                 "CreatedBy":"212.205.224.198",
                                 "CreatedOn":"/Date(1464952667680+0100)/",
                                 "UpdatedBy":"212.205.224.198",
                                 "UpdatedOn":"/Date(1464952667680+0100)/",
                                 "ImportOperation":null
                              },
                              "Segment":null
                           }
                        ],
                        "TotalSent":1,
                        "TotalOpens":1,
                        "UniqueOpens":1,
                        "TotalBounces":0,
                        "TotalForwards":0,
                        "UniqueForwards":0,
                        "TotalLinkClicks":0,
                        "UniqueLinkClicks":0,
                        "RecipientsCount":1,
                        "IsTransactional":false,
                        "TotalComplaints":0,
                        "TotalUnsubscribes":0
                     },
