## Creating & Managing Campaigns [/campaigns/{CampaignID}/clone.{Format}{?apikey}]

### Cloning An Existing Campaign [POST /campaigns/{CampaignID}/clone.{Format}{?apikey}]
Creates an exact copy of an existing campaign. The new campaign is created as a draft.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + CampaignID: `cbcb297d-52a8-4bed-ae85-640c37c92771` (required, string)
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.


+ Response 200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : This contains all the following information for the new campaign.
    + `ID` : The campaign id of the cloned campaign.
    + `Name` : The name of the campaign.  
    + `Subject`: The subject of the campaign.
    + `WebLocation`: The web location of your html campaign.
    + `HTMLContent` : The html content of the campaign.
    + `PlainContent` : The content of the campaign represented as a plain text. 
    + `Sender` : Contains all the information for the campaign sender.
        - `ID` : The id of the sender.
        - `Name` : The name of the sender.
        - `Email` : The email of the sender.
        - `CreatedOn` : The date that the sender was created.
        - `IsEnabled` : This will be true of false depending if the sender is enabled.
        - `SpfVerified` : This will be true of false depending if the spf records for this sender are enabled.
        - `DkimVerified` : This will be true of false depending if the dkim records for this sender are enabled.
        - `DkimPublic` : The sender email public dkim.
    + `DeliveredOn` : The date time that the campaign is delivered. Will be null in this case for the cloned campaign.
    + `ReplyToEmail` : Contains all the information for the reply to email.
        - `ID` : The id of the sender.
        - `Name` : The name of the sender.
        - `Email` : The email of the sender.
        - `CreatedOn` : The date that the sender was created.
        - `IsEnabled` : This will be true of false depending if the sender is enabled.
        - `SpfVerified` : This will be true of false depending if the spf records for this sender are enabled.
        - `DkimVerified` : This will be true of false depending if the dkim records for this sender are enabled.
        - `DkimPublic` : The reply email public dkim.
    + `CreatedOn` : The date time that the campaign was created.
    + `UpdatedOn` : The date time that the campaign was updated.
    + `ScheduleFor` : The date time that the campaign is scheduled to be delivered. Will be null for cloned campaigns.
    + `TimeZone` : The selected timezone for the account.
    + `FormatType` : The format type of the campaign. This will be 0 for Html, 1 for Template and 2 for PlainText.
    + `ABCampaignData` : This will be null for a regular campaign.
    + `ABCampaignData` : This will be null if the cloned campaign is a regular campaign. If it is an A/B split campaign it will contain all the following information :
        - `ID` : This is the ID of the ABCampaignData. It is a four digit integer.
        - `SubjectB` : If the A/B split campaign is testing the subject, this will be the subject line for the B campaign.
        - `PlainContentB` : If the A/B split campaign is testing the content, this will be the plain text content for the B campaign.
        - `HTMLContentB` : If the A/B split campaign is testing the content, this will be the html content for the B campaign.
        - `WebLocationB` : If the A/B split campaign is testing the content, this will be the web location for the B campaign.
        - `SenderB` : If the A/B split campaign is testing the sender, this will be the sender for the B campaign.
        - `HoursToTest` : The total number of hours to test version A and B of your campaign before sending the winning version.
        - `ListPercentage` : What is the size of your test group in your list.
        - `ABCampaignType` : The type of the A/B split campaign. This will be 0 for Sender, 1 for Content and 2 for Subject line.
        - `ABWinnerSelectionType` : The type of the test that will define the winner campaign. Will be 0 for unique opens test and 1 for unique clicks test.
        - `DeliveredOnA`: The date time that the campaign A was delivered. Will be null in this case for the cloned campaign.
        - `DeliveredOnB` : The date time that the campaign B was delivered. Will be null in this case for the cloned campaign.
    + `MailingLists` : A list that contains the mailing lists selected for this campaign to be sent to.
        - `MailingListID` : The ID of the mailing list.
        - `SegmentID` : The ID of the selected segment. Will be 0 if there is no segment selected.
    + `ConfirmationTo` : The confirmation to email.
    + `Status` : The status of the campaign. The clone campaign has 0 for status.
    + `IsTransactional` : Represents if the campaign was created using Smtp or not. It can be true or false.


    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json

    
    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": {
                "ID": "248f97f5-1e5f-4e17-8fa8-818dc112be10",
                "Name": "Test",
                "Subject": "Test",
                "WebLocation": "http:\/\/www.your-domain.com\/newsletter",
                "HTMLContent": "Some html content",
                "PlainContent": "Plain context ... ", 
                "Sender": {
                  "ID": "e9d2ed56-fc20-4337-bb6a-8b5884e8dfa6",
                  "Name": "Test",
                  "Email": "test@moosend.com",
                  "CreatedOn": "/Date(1457526079160+0100)/",
                  "IsEnabled": true,
                  "SpfVerified": false,
                  "DkimVerified": true,
                  "DkimPublic": "sender email dkim public"
                },
                "DeliveredOn": null,
                "ReplyToEmail": {
                  "ID": "21234a-cede-1234-1234-1bd8d7a46d2d",
                  "Name": "Andreas",
                  "Email": "andreas@moosend.com",
                  "CreatedOn": "/Date(1457526079160+0100)/",
                  "IsEnabled": true,
                  "SpfVerified": false,
                  "DkimVerified": true,
                  "DkimPublic": "reply to email dkim public"
                },
                "CreatedOn": "/Date(1469541491211)/",
                "UpdatedOn": "/Date(1469541491211)/",
                "ScheduledFor": null,
                "Timezone": "Korea Standard Time",
                "FormatType": 0,
                "ABCampaignData": {
                  "ID": 4080,
                  "SubjectB": "B Subject",
                  "PlainContentB": null,
                  "HTMLContentB": null,
                  "WebLocationB": null,
                  "SenderB": null,
                  "HoursToTest": 3,
                  "ListPercentage": 19,
                  "ABCampaignType": 2,
                  "ABWinnerSelectionType": 1,
                  "DeliveredOnA": null,
                  "DeliveredOnB": null
                },
                "MailingLists": [
                  {
                    "MailingListID": "e9d2ed56-fc20-4337-bb6a-8b5884e8dfa6",
                    "SegmentID": 0
                  }
                ],
                "ConfirmationTo": "test@moosend.com",
                "Status": 0,
                "IsTransactional": false
              }
            }


### Creating A Draft Campaign [POST /campaigns/create.{Format}{?apikey}]
Creates a new campaign in your account. This method does not send the campaign, but rather creates it as a draft, ready for sending or testing. 
You can choose to send either a regular campaign or an AB split campaign. Campaign content must be specified from a web location. 
Ignore ***(A/B Split Campaign Option)*** if you want to create a regular campaign.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.


+ Request (application/json)


    + `Name` : The name of the campaign. ***(Required)***
    + `Subject` : The subject line of the new campaign. ***(Required)***
    + `SenderEmail` : The sender email of the campaign. ***(Required)***
    + `ReplyToEmail` : The email address to which recipients replies will arrive. It must be one of your sender accounts. If not specified, the sender's email will be assumed. ***(Required)***
    + `ConfirmationToEmail` : The email address to which a confirmation message will be sent when the campaign has been successfully sent. 
    This can be any valid email address. It does not have to be one of your sender signatures. If not specified, the sender's email will be assumed. ***(Optional)***
    + `WebLocation` : A url to retrieve the html content for the campaign. We'll automatically move all CSS inline. ***(Optional)***
    + `MailingLists` : A list of mailing lists in your account to which the campaign will be sent to. ***(Optional)***
    + `SegmentID` : The ID of a segment in the specified mailing list to filter the recipients with. If not specified, the campaign will be sent to all active subscribers of the mailing list. ***(Optional)***
    + `IsAB` : A flag that defines if a campaign is an AB campaign. ***(Required)***
    + `ABCampaignType` : ***(A/B Split Campaign Option)*** If you want to send an AB split campaign you should specify this parameter to one of the following values. ***(Required)***
        * `Subjectline` : For testing two different versions of the subject line and send the final campaign to the one performing better.
        * `Content` : For testing two different versions of the campaign content and send the final campaign to the one performing better.
        * `Sender` : For testing two different versions of the sender name and send the final campaign to the one performing better.

    + `TrackInGoogleAnalytics` : Tracks traffic from your campaign to your site. Note: You need to have Google Analytics configured on your site to use this feature. ***(Optional)***
    + `SubjectB` : ***(A/B Split Campaign Option)*** If you wish to send an AB split campaign with two different versions of the subject line (ABCampaignType=Subject), 
    you must specify the second subject using this parameter. If specified in any other campaign type, it will be ignored. ***(Optional)***
    + `WebLocationB` : ***(A/B Split Campaign Option)*** If you wish to send an AB split campaign with two different versions of the html content (ABCampaignType=Content), 
    you must specify where the second html content will be retrieved from using this parameter. If specified in any other campaign type, it will be ignored. ***(Optional)***
    + `SenderEmailB` : ***(A/B Split Campaign Option)*** If you wish to send an AB split campaign with two different versions of the sender (ABCampaignType=Sender), 
    you must specify the second sender email address using this parameter. This must be one of your sender signatures defined in your account. If specified in any other campaign type, it will be ignored. ***(Optional)***
    + `HoursToTest` : ***(A/B Split Campaign Option)*** If you choose to send an AB campaign type, you must set this parameter to specify how long the test will run, before determining which will be the winning version to be sent to the rest of the recipients. 
    This should be an integer value between 1 and 24. If specified in a regular campaign, it will be ignored. ***(Optional)***
    + `ListPercentage` : ***(A/B Split Campaign Option)*** If you choose to send an AB campaign type, you must set this parameter to specify a portion of the target recipients that will receive the test versions. For example, if you specify 10, then 10% of your recipients will receive the A version and another 10% will receive the B version. 
    The specified value should be an integer between 5 and 40. If specified in a regular campaign, it will be ignored. ***(Optional)***
    + `ABWinnerSelectionType` : ***(A/B Split Campaign Option)*** If you choose to send an AB campaign type, you may set this parameter to one of the following values to specify the method to determine the winning version for the test. ***(Optional)*** <br/> If not set, OpenRate will be assumed. If specified in a regular campaign, it will be ignored.
        * `OpenRate` : To determine the winner according to which version achieved more opens.
        * `TotalUniqueClicks` : To determine the winner according to which version achieved more unique link clicks.

    
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body

            {
                "Name":"Test campaign",
                "Subject":"Some subject",
                "SenderEmail":"something@email.com",
                "ReplyToEmail":"something@email.com",
                "ConfirmationToEmail":"something@email.com",
                "WebLocation":"http://www.mysite.gr/newsletter/index",
                "MailingLists": [
                    {
                        "MailingListID":"adaf2fe1-55db-42dc-aaf8-56d8f502138d",
                        "SegmentID":"10166"
                    },
                    {
                        "MailingListID":"dce99b7a-2619-4805-aaeb-7fecdcb3c71b"
                    }
                ],
                "IsAB":"true",
                "ABCampaignType":"Content",
                "WebLocationB":"http://www.mysite.gr/newsletter/index",
                "HoursToTest":"2",
                "ListPercentage":"20",
                "ABWinnerSelectionType":"OpenRate"
            }
    
    

+ Response 200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : Contains the id of the new campaign.

    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": "afdc4ef6-999f-4d74-905b-ec234789f9d6"
            }

            
### Updating A Draft Campaign [POST /campaigns/{CampaignID}/update.{Format}{?apikey}]
Updates properties of an existing draft A/B campaign in your account. Non-draft campaigns cannot be updated.
Ignore ***(A/B Split Campaign Option)*** if you want to create a regular campaign.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.

+ Request (application/json)


    + `Name` : The name of the campaign. ***(Optional)***
    + `Subject` : The subject line of the new campaign. ***(Optional)***
    + `SenderEmail` : The sender email of the campaign. ***(Optional)***
    + `ReplyToEmail` : The email address to which recipients replies will arrive. It must be one of your sender accounts. If not specified, the sender's email will be assumed. ***(Optional)***
    + `ConfirmationToEmail` : The email address to which a confirmation message will be sent when the campaign has been successfully sent. 
    This can be any valid email address. It does not have to be one of your sender signatures. If not specified, the sender's email will be assumed. ***(Optional)***
    + `WebLocation` : A url to retrieve the html content for the campaign. We'll automatically move all CSS inline. ***(Optional)***
    + `MailingLists` : A list of mailing lists in your account to which the campaign will be sent to. ***(Optional)***
    + `SegmentID` : The ID of a segment in the specified mailing list to filter the recipients with. If not specified, the campaign will be sent to all active subscribers of the mailing list. ***(Optional)***
    + `IsAB` : A flag that defines if a campaign is an AB campaign. ***(Optional)***
    + `ABCampaignType` : ***(A/B Split Campaign Option)*** If you want to send an AB split campaign you should specify this parameter to one of the following values. ***(Optional)***
        * `Subjectline` : For testing two different versions of the subject line and send the final campaign to the one performing better
        * `Content` : For testing two different versions of the campaign content and send the final campaign to the one performing better
        * `Sender` : For testing two different versions of the sender name and send the final campaign to the one performing better

    + `TrackInGoogleAnalytics` : Tracks traffic from your campaign to your site. Note: You need to have Google Analytics configured on your site to use this feature. ***(Optional)***
    + `SubjectB` : ***(A/B Split Campaign Option)*** If you wish to send an AB split campaign with two different versions of the subject line (ABCampaignType=Subject), 
    you must specify the second subject using this parameter. If specified in any other campaign type, it will be ignored.
    + `WebLocationB` : ***(A/B Split Campaign Option)*** If you wish to send an AB split campaign with two different versions of the html content (ABCampaignType=Content), 
    you must specify where the second html content will be retrieved from using this parameter. If specified in any other campaign type, it will be ignored.
    + `SenderEmailB` : ***(A/B Split Campaign Option)*** If you wish to send an AB split campaign with two different versions of the sender (ABCampaignType=Sender), 
    you must specify the second sender email address using this parameter. This must be one of your sender signatures defined in your account. If specified in any other campaign type, it will be ignored.
    + `HoursToTest` : ***(A/B Split Campaign Option)*** If you choose to send an AB campaign type, you must set this parameter to specify how long the test will run, before determining which will be the winning version to be sent to the rest of the recipients.  
    This should be an integer value between 1 and 24. If specified in a regular campaign, it will be ignored. ***(Optional)***
    + `ListPercentage` : ***(A/B Split Campaign Option)*** If you choose to send an AB campaign type, you must set this parameter to specify a portion of the target recipients that will receive the test versions. For example, if you specify 10, then 10% of your recipients will receive the A version and another 10% will receive the B version. 
    The specified value should be an integer between 5 and 40. If specified in a regular campaign, it will be ignored. ***(Optional)***
    + `ABWinnerSelectionType` : ***(A/B Split Campaign Option)*** If you choose to send an AB campaign type, you may set this parameter to one of the following values to specify the method to determine the winning version for the test. ***(Optional)*** <br/> If not set, OpenRate will be assumed. If specified in a regular campaign, it will be ignored.
        * `OpenRate` : To determine the winner according to which version achieved more opens.
        * `TotalUniqueClicks` : To determine the winner according to which version achieved more unique link clicks.

    
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body

            {
                "Name":"Test campaign",
                "Subject":"Some subject",
                "SenderEmail":"something@email.com",
                "ReplyToEmail":"something@email.com",
                "ConfirmationToEmail":"something@email.com",
                "WebLocation":"http://www.mysite.gr/newsletter/index",
                "MailingLists": [
                    {
                        "MailingListID":"adaf2fe1-55db-42dc-aaf8-56d8f502138d",
