    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : The response context for this call. This will be null.

    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": null
            }


## Testing a campaign [/campaigns/{CampaignID}/send_test.{Format}{?apikey}]

### Testing a campaign [POST /campaigns/{CampaignID}/send_test.{Format}{?apikey}]
Sends a test email of a draft campaign to a list of email addresses you specify for previewing.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + CampaignID: `afdc4ef6-999f-4d74-905b-ec234789f9d6` (required, string)
    The ID of the draft campaign to be tested.

    
+ Request (application/json)


    + `TestEmails` : A list of email addresses to send the preview to (maximum 5 recipients, separated by commas). ***(Required)***
    
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
            
    + Body
    
            {
                "TestEmails":
                [
                    "email1@email.com",
                    "email2@email.com"
                ]
            }

+ Response 200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : The response context for this call. This will be null.
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
            
    + Body
    
            {   
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": null
            
            }
            
## Sending a campaign [/campaigns/{CampaignID}/send.{Format}{?apikey}]

### Sending a campaign [POST /campaigns/{CampaignID}/send.{Format}{?apikey}]
Sends an existing draft campaign to all recipients specified in its mailing list. The campaign is sent immediatelly.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + CampaignID: `afdc4ef6-999f-4d74-905b-ec234789f9d6` (required, string)
    The ID of the draft campaign to be sent.

        
+ Response 200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : The response context for this call. This will be null if successful.

    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": null
            }

        
## Getting Campaign Statistics [/campaigns/{CampaignID}/stats/{Type}.{Format}{?apikey}]

### Get Campaign Statistics [GET /campaigns/{CampaignID}/stats/{Type}.{Format}{?apikey}]
Returns a detailed list of statistics for a given campaign based on activity such as emails sent, opened, bounced, link clicked, etc. 
Because the results for this call could be quite big, paging information is required as input.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + CampaignID: `afdc4ef6-999f-4d74-905b-ec234789f9d6` (required, string)
    The ID of the requested AB test campaign
    + Type: Sent (optional, enum[string])
    The type of the activity to display results for. This must be one of the following values:
        * Sent: To get information about when and to which recipients the campaign was sent.
        * Opened: To get information about who opened the campaign.
        * LinkClicked: To get information about who clicked on which link.
        * Forward: To get information about who forwarded the campaign using the relevant link on the email body and when.
        * Unsubscribed : To get information about who unsubscribed from the campaign by clicking on the unsubscribe link and when.
        * Bounced : To get information about which email recipients failed to receive the campaign.
        If not specified, the value Sent will be used by default.
        
        + Members
            + Sent
            + Opened
            + LinkClicked
            + Forward
            + Unsubscribed
            + Bounced
    
    
+ Response 200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : This contains all the following for the campaign :
        - `Paging` : A list with all the following paging information:
            - `PageSize` : The page size of the results. This will be 0 if not defined.
            - `CurrentPage` : The number of the result page. This will be 1 if not defined.
            - `Totalresults` : The number of all the mailing lists that are included in the response.
            - `TotalPageCount` : The number of all the available mailing list pages for your account.
            - `SortExpression` : The sort expression associated with the column or columns being sorted.
            - `SortIsAscending` : This will be false if the results are not displayed with an ascending order based on the sort expression.
        - `Analytics` :  Contains a list of recipients with the following information:
            - `Context` : The email of the recipient.
            - `ContextName` : The name of the recipient.
            - `TotalCount` : The total number of type statistics produced by this recipient. This can be opens, link clicks etc. depending on the Type that you selected at the url.
            - `UniqueCount` : The unique number of type statistics produced by this recipient. This can be opens, link clicks etc. depending on the Type that you selected at the url.
            - `ContextDescription` : If selected type is unsubscribed, ContextDescription will contain the date time that the recipient unsubscribed from the campaign.
        
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": {
                "Paging": {
                  "PageSize": 1,
                  "CurrentPage": 1,
                  "TotalResults": 2,
                  "TotalPageCount": 1,
                  "SortExpression": null,
                  "SortIsAscending": false
                },
                "Analytics": [
                  {
                    "Context": "recipient@email.com",
                    "ContextName": "recipient name",
                    "TotalCount": 1,
                    "UniqueCount": 0,
                    "ContextDescription": null
                  },
                    {
                    "Context": "recipient2@email.com",
                    "ContextName": "recipient2 name",
                    "TotalCount": 1,
                    "UniqueCount": 0,
                    "ContextDescription": null
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
    
### Get Campaign Statistics With Paging & Filtered  [GET /campaigns/{CampaignID}/stats/{Type}.{Format}{?apikey}{?Page}{?PageSize}{?From}{?To}]
Returns a detailed list of statistics for a given campaign based on activity such as emails sent, opened, bounced, link clicked, etc. 
Because the results for this call could be quite big, paging information is required as input.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + CampaignID: `afdc4ef6-999f-4d74-905b-ec234789f9d6` (required, string)
    The ID of the requested AB test campaign
    + Page: 1 (optional, string)
    The page number to display results for. If not specified, the first page will be returned.
    + PageSize: 1 (optional, string)
    The maximum number of results per page. This must be a positive integer up to 100. If not specified, 50 results per page will be returned. 
    If a value greater than 100 is specified, it will be treated as 100.
    + Type: Sent (optional, enum[string])
    The type of the activity to display results for. This must be one of the following values :
        * Sent : To get information about when and to which recipients the campaign was sent.
        * Opened : To get information about who opened the campaign.
        * LinkClicked : To get information about who clicked on which link.
        * Forward : To get information about who forwarded the campaign using the relevant link on the email body and when.
        * Unsubscribed : To get information about who unsubscribed from the campaign by clicking on the unsubscribe link and when.
        * Bounced : To get information about which email recipients failed to receive the campaign.
        If not specified, the value Sent will be used by default.
        * Complained : To get information about which email recipients have reported your newsletter as spam through their email service.
        
        + Members
            + Sent
            + Opened
            + LinkClicked
            + Forward
            + Unsubscribed
            + Bounced
            + Complained
    + From: `11-06-2016` (optional, string)
    A date value that specifies since when to start returning results. If omitted, results will be returned from the moment the campaign was sent.
    + To: `16-06-2016` (optional, string)
    A date value that specifies up to when to return results. If omitted, results will be returned up to date.
    
    
+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : This contains all the following for the campaign :
        - `Paging` : A list with all the following paging information:
            - `PageSize` : The page size of the results. This will be 0 if not defined.
            - `CurrentPage` : The number of the result page. This will be 1 if not defined.
            - `Totalresults` : The number of all the mailing lists that are included in the response.
            - `TotalPageCount` : The number of all the available mailing list pages for your account.
            - `SortExpression` : The sort expression associated with the column or columns being sorted.
            - `SortIsAscending` : This will be false if the results are not displayed with an ascending order based on the sort expression.
        - `Analytics` :  Contains a list of recipients with the following information:
            - `Context` : The email of the recipient.
            - `ContextName` : The name of the recipient.
            - `TotalCount` : The total number of type statistics produced by this recipient. This can be opens, link clicks etc. depending on the Type that you selected at the url.
            - `UniqueCount` : The unique number of type statistics produced by this recipient. This can be opens, link clicks etc. depending on the Type that you selected at the url.
            - `ContextDescription` : If selected type is unsubscribed, ContextDescription will contain the date time that the recipient unsubscribed from the campaign.
        
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": {
                "Paging": {
                  "PageSize": 5,
                  "CurrentPage": 1,
                  "TotalResults": 374,
                  "TotalPageCount": 75,
                  "SortExpression": null,
                  "SortIsAscending": false
                },
                "Analytics": [
                  {
                    "Context": "recipient1@email.com",
                    "ContextName": "",
                    "TotalCount": 1,
                    "UniqueCount": 0,
                    "ContextDescription": null
                  },
                  {
                    "Context": "recipient2@email.com",
                    "ContextName": "Paul",
                    "TotalCount": 1,
                    "UniqueCount": 0,
                    "ContextDescription": null
                  },
                  {
                    "Context": "recipient3@email.com",
                    "ContextName": "John",
                    "TotalCount": 5,
                    "UniqueCount": 0,
                    "ContextDescription": null
                  },
                  {
                    "Context": "recipient4@email.com",
                    "ContextName": "Marc",
                    "TotalCount": 4,
                    "UniqueCount": 0,
                    "ContextDescription": null
                  },
                  {
                    "Context": "recipient5@email.com",
                    "ContextName": "",
                    "TotalCount": 3,
                    "UniqueCount": 0,
                    "ContextDescription": null
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
    
### Campaign Summary [GET /campaigns/{CampaignID}/view_summary.{Format}{?apikey}]
Provides a basic summary of the results for any sent campaign such as the number of recipients, opens, clicks, bounces, unsubscribes, forwards etc. to date.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + CampaignID: `afdc4ef6-999f-4d74-905b-ec234789f9d6` (required, string)
    The ID of the requested campaign
    
        
+ Response 200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : Contains all the following information for the given campaign:
        - `CampaignID` : The campaign id.
        - `ABVersion` : If the campaign is an A/B split test campaign, this will display which version was sent. Will be null if it is a normal campaign.
        - `CampaignName` : The name of the campaign.
        - `CampaignSubject` : The subject line of the campaign.
        - `MailingLists` : Contains a list of mailing lists and segments, to which the campaign was sent to. We can see the following information for each mailing list or segment:
            - `MailingListID`: The ID of the mailing list that the campaign was sent to.
            - `SegmentID` : The ID of the segment that the campaign was sent to. This will be null if the campaign was not sent to a segment.
        - `CampaignDeliveredOn` : The date time that the campaign 
        - `To` : The date time that the measurement ended.
        - `From` : The date time that the measurement started.
        - `TotalOpens` : The number of the total opens for the given campaign.
        - `UniqueOpens` : The number of the total unique opens for the given campaign.
        - `TotalBounces` : The number of the total bounces for the given campaign.
        - `TotalComplaints` : The number of the total complaints for the given campaign.
        - `TotalForwards` : The number of the total forwards for the given campaign. This will count emails forwarded by the "Forward to a friend" personalization tag only.
        - `UniqueForwards` : The number of the total unique forwards for the given campaign. This will count emails forwarded by the "Forward to a friend" personalization tag only.
        - `TotalUnsubscribes` : The number of the total unsubscribed recipients for the given campaign.
        - `TotalLinkClicks` : The number of the total link clicks for the given campaign.
        - `UniqueLinkClicks` : The number of the total unique link clicks for the given campaign.
        - `Sent` : The number of the total sent emails.
        - `CampaignIsArchived` : Campaigns that are older than 3 months get Archived and only high-level data are available for this campaign.
        
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": {
                "CampaignID": "13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32",
                "ABVersion": null,
                "CampaignName": "test image path",
                "CampaignSubject": "test image path",
                "MailingLists": [
                  {
                    "MailingListID": "84bs231b131-367a-4d73-af11-01b4b45d3f54",
                    "SegmentID": 0
                  }
                ],
                "CampaignDeliveredOn": "/Date(1464256291013+0100)/",
                "To": "/Date(1465481260987+0100)/",
                "From": "/Date(1464256291013+0100)/",
                "TotalOpens": 1340,
                "UniqueOpens": 780,
                "TotalBounces": 4,
                "TotalComplaints": 0,
                "TotalForwards": 55,
                "UniqueForwards": 55,
                "TotalUnsubscribes": 7,
                "TotalLinkClicks": 976,
                "UniqueLinkClicks": 711,
                "Sent": 2550,
                "CampaignIsArchived": false
              }
            }

### Activity By Location [GET /campaigns/{CampaignID}/stats/countries.{Format}{?apikey}]
Returns a detailed report of your campaign opens (unique and total) by country.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + CampaignID: `afdc4ef6-999f-4d74-905b-ec234789f9d6` (required, string)
    The ID of the requested campaign

        
+ Response 200 (application/json)


    
    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : This contains all the following for the campaign :
        - `Paging` : A list with all the following paging information:
            - `PageSize` : The page size of the results. This will be 0 if not defined.
            - `CurrentPage` : The number of the result page. This will be 1 if not defined.
            - `Totalresults` : The number of all the mailing lists that are included in the response.
            - `TotalPageCount` : The number of all the available mailing list pages for your account.
            - `SortExpression` : The sort expression associated with the column or columns being sorted.
            - `SortIsAscending` : This will be false if the results are not displayed with an ascending order based on the sort expression.
        - `Analytics` :  Contains a list of countries with the following information:
            - `Context` : The country code.
            - `ContextName` : The name of the country.
            - `TotalCount` : The total number of campaign opens.
            - `UniqueCount` : The unique number of campaign opens.
            - `ContextDescription` : Will be null for this case.
        
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": {
                "Paging": {
                  "PageSize": 0,
                  "CurrentPage": 1,
                  "TotalResults": 0,
                  "TotalPageCount": 0,
                  "SortExpression": null,
                  "SortIsAscending": false
                },
                "Analytics": [
                  {
                    "Context": "  ",
                    "ContextName": null,
                    "TotalCount": 1,
                    "UniqueCount": 1,
                    "ContextDescription": null
                  }
                ]
              }
            }

### Link Activity [GET /campaigns/{CampaignID}/stats/links.{Format}{?apikey}]
Returns a list with your campaign links and how many clicks have been made by your recipients, either unique or total.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + CampaignID: `afdc4ef6-999f-4d74-905b-ec234789f9d6` (required, string)
    The ID of the requested campaign

        
+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : This contains all the following for the campaign :
        - `Paging` : A list with all the following paging information:
            - `PageSize` : The page size of the results. This will be 0 if not defined.
            - `CurrentPage` : The number of the result page. This will be 1 if not defined.
            - `Totalresults` : The number of all the mailing lists that are included in the response.
            - `TotalPageCount` : The number of all the available mailing list pages for your account.
            - `SortExpression` : The sort expression associated with the column or columns being sorted.
            - `SortIsAscending` : This will be false if the results are not displayed with an ascending order based on the sort expression.
        - `Analytics` :  Contains a list of links that exist in the given campaign, with the following information:
            - `Context` : Contains the url.
            - `ContextName` : Will be null.
            - `TotalCount` : The total number of link clicks.
            - `UniqueCount` : The unique number of link clicks.
            - `ContextDescription` : Will be null.
        
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
    
            {  
               "Code":0,
               "Error":null,
               "Context":{  
                  "Paging":{  
                     "PageSize":0,
                     "CurrentPage":1,
                     "TotalResults":0,
                     "TotalPageCount":0,
                     "SortExpression":null,
                     "SortIsAscending":false
                  },
                  "Analytics":[  
                     {  
                        "Context":"http://someUrl.com/",
