              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": null
            }

### A/B Test Campaign Summary [GET /campaigns/{CampaignID}/view_ab_summary.{Format}{?apikey}]
Provides a basic summary of the results for a sent AB test campaign, separately for each version (A and B), such as the number of recipients, opens, clicks, bounces, unsubscribes, forwards etc to date.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + CampaignID: `afdc4ef6-999f-4d74-905b-ec234789f9d6` (required, string)
    The ID of the requested AB test campaign

    
+ Response 200 (application/json)

    
    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error `: The response error message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : Contains all the following information for the A/B split test campaign :
        + `CampaignID` : The id of the winner campaign.
        + `A` : Contains the following information for campaign A :
            + `CampaignID` : The id of A campaign.
            + `ABVersion` : The version of the campaign. Will be `0` for A and `1` for B.
            + `CampaignName` : The name of the campaign.  
            + `CampaignSubject` : The subject of the campaign.
            + `MailingLists` : Contains a list of mailing lists and segments, that the campaign was sent to.
                + `Campaign` : Will be null for this case.
                + `ID` : The id of the mailing list.
                + `Name` : The name of the mailing list.
                + `ActiveMemberCount` : The number of the active members for the mailing list.
                + `BouncedMemberCount` : The number of the bounced emails for the mailing list.
                + `RemovedMemberCount` : The number of the removed emails for the mailing list.
                + `UnsubscribedMemberCount` : The number of the unsubscribed emails for the mailing list.
                + `Status` : The status of the mailing list.
                    - `0` is for created.
                    - `1` is for imported. 
                    - `2` is for importing. 
                    - `3` is for deleted.
                + `CustomFieldsDefinition` : The details of each custom field for the mailing list. This will be blank if there are no custom fields for this mailing list.
                    - `ID` : The id of the custom field.
                    - `Name` : The name of the custom field.
                    - `Context` : The context of the custom field. Will be null if not singleSelectDropDown.
                    - `IsRequired` : False if the custom field is not required, true if it is.
                    - `Type` : The type of the custom field.
                        - `0` for text 
                        - `1` for decimal 
                        - `2` for dateTime 
                        - `3` for singleSelectDropDown 
                        - `4` for integer 
                        - `5` for checkbox
                + `CreatedBy` : The ip from where the mailing list was created.
                + `CreatedOn` : The date time that the mailing list was created.
                + `UpdatedBy` : The ip from where the mailing list was updated.
                + `UpdatedOn` : The date time that the mailing list was updated.
                + `ImportOperation` : The details of the latest import operation that was performed in the mailing list.
                     - `ID` : The id of the import operation.
                     - `DataHash` : A guid id for the import operation.
                     - `Mappings` : The mappings that where used for the specific import operation (Email, Name etc.).
                     - `EmailNotify` : Null if the import operation notification email was not selected to be sent.
                     - `CreatedOn` : The date time that the import operation was created.
                     - `StartedOn` : The date time that the import operation started.
                     - `CompletedOn` : The date time that the import operation was completed.
                     - `TotalInserted` : The number of the total inserted emails.
                     - `TotalUpdated` : The number of the total emails that where updated.
                     - `TotalUnsubscribed` : The number of the total emails that where unsubscribed.
                     - `TotalInvalid` : The number of the total invalid emails.
                     - `TotalIgnored` : The number of the total ignored emails.
                     - `TotalDuplicate` : The number of the total duplicate emails.
                     - `TotalMembers` : The number of the total members that where selected to be imported.
                     - `Message` : The message of the import operation. This will be null if successful.
                     - `Success` : This will be true if successful.
                     - `SkipNewMembers` : This will be false if the skip new members option was not selected before the import operation began.
                + `Segment` : A list with all the following information for the given segment. Will be null if the campaign was not sent to a segment of this mailing list.
                     - `ID` : The id of the segment.
                     - `Name` : The name of the segment.
                     - `MatchType` :  The match criteria selected for this segment. This will be:
                        - `0` : For All.
                        - `1` : For Any.
                     - `Criteria` : A list with all the selected criteria for this segment.
                     - `CreatedBy`: The ip from where the segment was created.
                     - `CreatedOn` : The date time that the segment was created.
                     - `UpdatedBy` : The ip from where the segment was updated.
                     - `UpdatedOn` : The date time that the segment was updated.
                     - `FetchType` : The selected fetch type for the selected segment criteria. This will be:
                        - `0` : For all segment criteria.
                        - `1` : For top segment criteria.
                        - `2` : For top percent segment criteria.
                     - `Description` : Contains a string representation of all the selected filters, MatchType criteria and FetchType criteria.
            + `CampaignDeliveredOn` : The date time that the campaign 
            + `To` : The date time that the measurement ended.
            + `From` : The date time that the measurement started.
            + `TotalOpens` : The number of the total opens for the given campaign.
            + `UniqueOpens` : The number of the total unique opens for the given campaign.
            + `TotalBounces` : The number of the total bounces for the given campaign.
            + `TotalComplaints` : The number of the total complaints for the given campaign.
            + `TotalForwards` : The number of the total forwards for the given campaign. This will count emails forwarded by the "Forward to a friend" personalization tag only.
            + `UniqueForwards` : The number of the total unique forwards for the given campaign. This will count emails forwarded by the "Forward to a friend" personalization tag only.
            + `TotalUnsubscribes` : The number of the total unsubscribed recipients for the given campaign.
            + `TotalLinkClicks` : The number of the total link clicks for the given campaign.
            + `UniqueLinkClicks` : The number of the total unique link clicks for the given campaign.
            + `Sent` : The number of the total sent emails.
            + `CampaignIsArchived` : Campaigns that are older than 3 months get Archived and only high-level data are available for this campaign.

    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body

