# Group Segments

The Segmentation Service allows you to retrieve or count mailing list members based on given criteria.
Combinations of criteria can be as complex as you want with nested AND / OR expressions.

## Segmentation Basics

A **segmentation query** (criterion) consists mainly of the following parts:
 1. The `query field`. A complete list of available fields follows.
 2. The `query operator` (comparer). Each field supports specific comparers based on its data type.
 3. The `value` to filter the query. It can be a single value or an array of values.
 4. Additional parameters when supported. Available parameters are listed below.

A **segmentation expression** consists of multiple queries than can be matched together in complex, nested combinations. The `MatchType` property defines how a group of queries (criteria) are combined.
 - `MatchType: All` means that members should match all criteria and is equivalent to AND logical operator.
 - `MatchType: Any` means that members should match any criteria and is equivalent to OR logical operator.

The `FetchType` property defines how many of the criteria matching subscribers will be contained in the created segment .
 - `FetchType: All` means that all criteria matching members will be contained in the created segment.
 - `FetchType: Top` means that only the maximum number of members defined in `FetchValue`will be contained in the created segment.
 - `FetchType: TopPercent` means that only the percentage of members defined in `FetchValue` will be contained in the created segment.
 - `FetchValue`: is used with `FetchType: Top` or `FetchType: TopPercent` to define the maximum number or percentage of members to be contained in the created segment.
 
### List of Segmentation Fields
Segmentation expressions can contain any combination of the following fields. You can use either the name of the code in your json request body. Some fields accept additional parameters.
 - `Date Constrain` parameters constrain the results based on a related date field
 - `OtherMailingListId` parameter executes the query on another mailing list on members that are contained on both the current and the other mailing list
 - `CustomFieldId` or `CustomFieldName` parameters is used only with field CustomField (99) and specifies the custom field definition by the id or the name for which the query applies. The custom field definition can be either one of the current mailing list or the mailing list specified by the `OtherMailingListId` parameter.
 
|Member Fields|Code|Data Type|Date Constrain|OtherMailingListId|
|--|--|--|--|--|
|DateAdded| 1 |DateTime|  | Yes |
|DateUpdated|16|DateTime|  | Yes |
|RecipientName|2|String|  | Yes |
|RecipientEmail|3|String|  |  |
|SubscribeMethod|14|Enum|Yes (SubscribedOn)|Yes|
|CustomField|99|String, Decimal, DateTime, Boolean|  |  Yes|
|MailingList|17|Guid|  |  |
 |**Campaign Fields**|**Code**|**Data Type**|**Date Constrain**|**OtherMailingListId**|
|CampaignsOpened|4|Integer|Yes (DeliveredOn)|Yes|
|LinksClicked|5|Integer|Yes (DeliveredOn)|Yes|
|CampaignName|6|String|Yes (DeliveredOn)|Yes|
|CampaignTitle|20|String|Yes (Timestamp)|Yes|
|LinkURL|7|Guid|Yes (DeliveredOn)|Yes|
|CampaignSent|15|Guid|Yes (Timestamp)|Yes|
|OpenedAnyCampaign|24|Boolean|Yes (Timestamp)|Yes|
|CampaignID|19|GUID|Yes (Timestamp)|Yes|
|SpecificCampaignClicked|26|String|Yes (Timestamp)|Yes|
|CampaignIdNotOpened|27|String|  |Yes|
 |**User Agent Fields**|**Code**|**Data Type**|**Date Constrain**|**OtherMailingListId**|
|Platform|8|Enum (Desktop = 1, Mobile = 2, Other = 3)|  |  |
|OperatingSystem|9|String|  |  |
|EmailClient|10|String|  |  |
|WebBrowser|11|String|  |  |
|MobileBrowser|12|String|  |  |
 |**Website Fields**|**Code**|**Data Type**|**Date Constrain**|**OtherMailingListId**|
|AddedAnythingToCart|21|Boolean + Extra (CampaignId, ProductCode, WebsiteId, Times)|Yes (Timestamp)|Yes|
|ViewedProduct|22|Boolean + Extra (CampaignId, ProductCode, WebsiteId, Times)|Yes (Timestamp)|Yes|
|PurchasedProduct|23|Boolean + Extra (CampaignId, ProductCode, WebsiteId, Times)|Yes (Timestamp)|Yes|
### List of Query Operators (Comparers)
Query operators differ according to the data type of the field. Below you find a complete list of supported operators per data type. You can use either the name of the code in your JSON request body.
> `IsEmpty*` and `IsNotEmpty*` are available when the field is nullable

|Operator|Code|String|Integer|Decimal|DateTime|Enum|Guid|Boolean|
|--|--|--|--|--|--|--|--|--|
|Is| 0 |+|+|+|+|+|+||
|IsNot|1|+|+|+|+|+|+||
|Contains|2|+|  |||||
|DoesNotContain|3|+|  |||||
|StartsWith|4|+|  |||||
|DoesNotStartWith|5|+  |  |||||
|EndsWith|6|+|  |||||
|DoesNotEndWith|7|+|||||||
|IsGreaterThan|8||+|+|||||
|IsGreaterThanOrEqualTo|9||+|+|||||
|IsLessThan|10||+|+|||||
|IsLessThanOrEqualTo|11||+|+|||||
|IsBefore|12||||+||||
|IsAfter|13||||+||||
|IsEmpty*|14|+|+|+|+|+|+|+|
|IsNotEmpty*|15|+|+|+|+|+|+|+|
|IsTrue|16|||||||+|
|IsFalse|17|||||||+|
|IsBetween|24||+|+|+||||
|IsNotBetween|25||+|+|+||||
### List of Date Functions
The following list of date functions can be used with fields of DateTime data type. You can query based on a property of the date instead of the date itself. Calculation depends on parameter TimeZoneUsed with possible values: Local, Utc. When Local is used, the user's timezone offset is taken into account.

|Function Name|Code|Description|
|--|--|--|
|Year|1|The year part of the date (4 digits)|
|Month|2|The month part of the date (1-12)|
|Day|3|The day part of the date (1-31)|
|WeekDay|4|The week day of the date (1-7, Sunday = 1, Monday = 2, etc)|
|DaysPassed|5|Number of days that have passed until now|
|HoursPassed|6|Number of hours that have passed until now|
|MinutesPassed|7|Number of minutes that have passed until now|
### List of Date Constrain Parameters
- `LastXMinutes` parameter constrains the results in relevance to the time that has elapsed
- `DateFrom` and `DateTo` parameters constrain the results based on a specific date span


## Getting segments [/segments/{SegmentID}/details.{Format}{?apikey}]

### Getting segments [GET /lists/{MailingListID}/segments.{Format}{?apikey}]
Get a list of all segments with their criteria for the given mailing list.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string)
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.

+ Response 200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful
    + `Context` : The response context. Contains all the following information:
        - `Paging` : A list with all the following paging information.
            - `PageSize` : The page size of the results. This will be 0 if not defined.
            - `CurrentPage` : The number of the result page. This will be 1 if not defined.
            - `Totalresults` : The number of all the mailing lists that are included in the response.
            - `TotalPageCount` : The number of all the available mailing list pages for your account.
            - `SortExpression` : The sort expression associated with the column or columns being sorted.
            - `SortIsAscending` : This will be false if the results are not displayed with an ascending order based on the sort expression.
        - `Segments` : A list with the following information for each segment for the given mailing list:
            - `ID` : The ID of the segment.
            - `Name` : The name of the segment.
            - `MatchType` : Specifies how the segment's criteria will match together. This can be one of the following values :
                - `0` : For All. Only subscribers that match all given criteria will be returned by the segment.
                - `1` : For Any.  Subscribers that match any of the given criteria will be returned by the segment.
            -`Criteria` : Contains a list with the following information for each selected criterion selected for this segment :
                - `ID` : The id of the criteria.
                - `SegmentID` : The ID of the segment.
                - `Field` : The enum value of the selected filter.
                - `CustomFieldID`: If the selected filter is a custom field this will be the custom fields ID.
                - `Comparer` : An operator that defines the way to compare a criterion field with its value. This must be one of the following values. ***(Optional)*** <br/> If not specified, `Is` will be assumed.
                    - `0` : For Is. To find subscribers where the field is exactly equal to the search term.
                    - `1` : For IsNot. To find subscribers where the field is other than the search term.
                    - `2` : For Contains. To find subscribers where the field contains the search term.
                    - `3` : For DoesNotContain. To find subscribers where the field does not contain the search term.
                    - `4` : For StartsWith. To find subscribers where the field starts with the search term.
                    - `5` : For DoesNotStartWith. To find subscribers where the field does not start with the search term.
                    - `6` : For EndsWith. To find subscribers where the field ends with the search term.
                    - `7`: For DoesNotEndWith. To find subscribers where the field does not end with the search term.
                    - `8` : For IsGreaterThan. To find subscribers where the field is greater than the search term.
                    - `9` : For IsGreaterThanOrEqualTo. To find subscribers where the field is greater than or equal to the search term.
                    - `10` : For IsLessThan. To find subscribers where the field is less than the search term.
                    - `11` : For IsLessThanOrEqualTo. To find subscribers where the field is less than or equal to the search term.
                    - `12` : For IsBefore. To find subscribers where the specified date field is before the specified date value.
                    - `13` : For IsAfter. To find subscribers where the specified date field is after the specified date value.
                    - `14` : For IsEmpty. To find subscribers where the field contains no value.
                    - `15` : For IsNotEmpty. To find subscribers excluding those where the field contains no value.
                    - `16` : For IsTrue. To find subscribers where the condition defined by the field is true.
                    - `17` : For IsFalse. To find subscribers where the condition defined by the field is false.
                    - `24` : For IsBetween. To find subscribers where the numeric value of a criteria is between the 2 defined numbers.
                    - `25` : For IsNotBetween. To find subscribers where the numeric value of a criteria is not between the 2 defined numbers.
                    
                - `Value` : The filter value.
                - `DateFrom` : The date time value selected for the filter to filter results from. If not selected will be null.
                - `DateTo` : The date time value selected for the filter to filter results to. If not selected will be null.
                - `Properties` : Will be null for this case.
                - `Subscriteria` :  Will be null for this case.
            - `CreatedBy`: The ip from where the segment was created.
            - `CreatedOn` : The date time that the segment was created.
            - `UpdatedBy` : The ip from where the segment was updated.
            - `UpdatedOn` : The date time that the segment was updated.
            - `FetchType` : The selected fetch type for the selected segment criteria. This will be:
                - `0` : For all segment criteria.
                - `1` : For top segment criteria.
                - `2` : For top percent segment criteria.
            - `FetchValue` : The value on which the FetchType filter will be applied.
            - `Description` : Contains a string representation of all the selected filters, MatchType criteria and FetchType criteria.


    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body

            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": {
                "Paging": {
                  "PageSize": 100,
                  "CurrentPage": 1,
                  "TotalResults": 1,
                  "TotalPageCount": 1,
                  "SortExpression": "CreatedOn",
                  "SortIsAscending": false
                },
                "Segments": [
                  {
                    "ID": 7314,
                    "Name": "City",
                    "MatchType": 1,
                    "Criteria": [
                      {
                        "ID": 12244,
                        "SegmentID": 7314,
                        "Field": 2,
                        "CustomFieldID": null,
                        "Comparer": 0,
                        "Value": "test",
                        "DateFrom": null,
                        "DateTo": null,
                        "Properties": null,
                        "Subscriteria": null
                      },
                      {
                        "ID": 12348,
                        "SegmentID": 7314,
                        "Field": 99,
                        "CustomFieldID": "e4823107-d02d-48af-8190-d8694a33401e",
                        "Comparer": 0,
                        "Value": "UK",
                        "DateFrom": null,
                        "DateTo": null,
                        "Properties": null,
                        "Subscriteria": null
                      }
                    ],
                    "CreatedBy": "211.11.111.11",
                    "CreatedOn": "/Date(1451490040010+0000)/",
                    "UpdatedBy": "211.11.111.11",
                    "UpdatedOn": "/Date(1451490040010+0000)/",
                    "FetchType": 0,
                    "FetchValue": 0,
                    "Description": "Fetch all where \"City\" is \"UK\" or \"Recipient Name\" is \"Test\""
                  }
                ]
              }
            }

### Getting segment details [GET /lists/{MailingListID}/segments/{SegmentID}/details.{Format}{?apikey}]
Gets detailed information on a specific segment and its criteria. However, it does not include the subscribers returned by the segment.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string)
    The ID of the mailing list the specified segment belongs
    + SegmentID: 10198 (required, string)
    The ID of the segment to fetch results for.
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.

+ Response 200 (application/json)



    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful
    + `Context` : The response context. Contains all the following information:
        - `Paging` : A list with all the following paging information.
            - `PageSize` : The page size of the results. This will be 0 if not defined.
            - `CurrentPage` : The number of the result page. This will be 1 if not defined.
            - `Totalresults` : The number of all the mailing lists that are included in the response.
            - `TotalPageCount` : The number of all the available mailing list pages for your account.
            - `SortExpression` : The sort expression associated with the column or columns being sorted.
            - `SortIsAscending` : This will be false if the results are not displayed with an ascending order based on the sort expression.
        - `Segments` : A list with the following information for each segment for the given mailing list:
            - `ID` : The ID of the segment.
            - `Name` : The name of the segment.
            - `MatchType` : Specifies how the segment's criteria will match together. This can be one of the following values :
                - `0` : For All. Only subscribers that match all given criteria will be returned by the segment.
                - `1` : For Any.  Subscribers that match any of the given criteria will be returned by the segment.
            -`Criteria` : Contains a list with the following information for each selected criterion selected for this segment :
                - `ID` : The id of the criteria.
                - `SegmentID` : The ID of the segment.
                - `Field` : The enum value of the selected filter.
                - `CustomFieldID`: If the selected filter is a custom field this will be the custom fields ID.
                - `Comparer` : An operator that defines the way to compare a criterion field with its value. This must be one of the following values. ***(Optional)*** <br/> If not specified, `Is` will be assumed.
                    - `0` : For Is. To find subscribers where the field is exactly equal to the search term.
                    - `1` : For IsNot. To find subscribers where the field is other than the search term.
                    - `2` : For Contains. To find subscribers where the field contains the search term.
                    - `3` : For DoesNotContain. To find subscribers where the field does not contain the search term.
                    - `4` : For StartsWith. To find subscribers where the field starts with the search term.
                    - `5` : For DoesNotStartWith. To find subscribers where the field does not start with the search term.
                    - `6` : For EndsWith. To find subscribers where the field ends with the search term.
                    - `7`: For DoesNotEndWith. To find subscribers where the field does not end with the search term.
                    - `8` : For IsGreaterThan. To find subscribers where the field is greater than the search term.
                    - `9` : For IsGreaterThanOrEqualTo. To find subscribers where the field is greater than or equal to the search term.
                    - `10` : For IsLessThan. To find subscribers where the field is less than the search term.
                    - `11` : For IsLessThanOrEqualTo. To find subscribers where the field is less than or equal to the search term.
                    - `12` : For IsBefore. To find subscribers where the specified date field is before the specified date value.
                    - `13` : For IsAfter. To find subscribers where the specified date field is after the specified date value.
                    - `14` : For IsEmpty. To find subscribers where the field contains no value.
                    - `15` : For IsNotEmpty. To find subscribers excluding those where the field contains no value.
                    - `16` : For IsTrue. To find subscribers where the condition defined by the field is true.
                    - `17` : For IsFalse. To find subscribers where the condition defined by the field is false.
                    - `24` : For IsBetween. To find subscribers where the numeric value of a criteria is between the 2 defined numbers.
                    - `25` : For IsNotBetween. To find subscribers where the numeric value of a criteria is not between the 2 defined numbers.
                - `Value` : The filter value.
                - `DateFrom` : The date time value selected for the filter to filter results from. If not selected will be null.
                - `DateTo` : The date time value selected for the filter to filter results to. If not selected will be null.
                - `Properties` : Will be null for this case.
                - `Subscriteria` :  Will be null for this case.
            - `CreatedBy`: The ip from where the segment was created.
            - `CreatedOn` : The date time that the segment was created.
            - `UpdatedBy` : The ip from where the segment was updated.
            - `UpdatedOn` : The date time that the segment was updated.
            - `FetchType` : The selected fetch type for the selected segment criteria. This will be:
                - `0` : For all segment criteria.
                - `1` : For top segment criteria.
                - `2` : For top percent segment criteria.
            - `FetchValue` : The value on which the FetchType filter will be applied.
            - `Description` : Contains a string representation of all the selected filters, MatchType criteria and FetchType criteria.



    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body

            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": {
                "ID": 10198,
                "Name": "test",
                "MatchType": 0,
                "Criteria": [
                  {
                    "ID": 15778,
                    "SegmentID": 10198,
                    "Field": 2,
                    "CustomFieldID": null,
                    "Comparer": 0,
                    "Value": "Paul",
                    "DateFrom": null,
                    "DateTo": null,
                    "Properties": null,
                    "Subscriteria": null
                  },
                  {
                    "ID": 15779,
                    "SegmentID": 10198,
                    "Field": 4,
                    "CustomFieldID": null,
                    "Comparer": 8,
                    "Value": "5",
                    "DateFrom": "/Date(1465167600000+0100)/",
                    "DateTo": "/Date(1465945200000+0100)/",
                    "Properties": null,
                    "Subscriteria": null
                  }
                ],
                "CreatedBy": "212.123.123.112",
                "CreatedOn": "/Date(1465806037033+0100)/",
                "UpdatedBy": "212.123.123.112",
                "UpdatedOn": "/Date(1465806269980+0100)/",
                "FetchType": 0,
                "FetchValue": 0,
                "Description": "Fetch all where \"Recipient Name\" is \"Paul\" and \"Campaigns Opened\" is greater than \"5\""
              }
            }

### Getting segment subscribers [GET /lists/{MailingListID}/segments/{SegmentID}/members.{Format}{?apikey}]
Gets a list of the subscribers that the specified segment returns according to its criteria. Because the results for this call could be quite big, paging information is required as input.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string)
    The ID of the mailing list the specified segment belongs
    + SegmentID: 10198 (required, string)
    The ID of the segment to fetch results for.
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful
    + `Error` : The response error message. This will be null if successful
    + `Context` : The response context. Contains all the following information:
        - `Paging` : A list with all the following paging information.
            - `PageSize` : The page size of the results. This will be 0 if not defined.
            - `CurrentPage` : The number of the result page. This will be 1 if not defined.
            - `Totalresults` : The number of all the mailing lists that are included in the response.
            - `TotalPageCount` : The number of all the available mailing list pages for your account.
            - `SortExpression` : The sort expression associated with the column or columns being sorted.
            - `SortIsAscending` : This will be false if the results are not displayed with an ascending order based on the sort expression.
        - `Subscribers` : A list with the following information for each subscriber for the given segment :
            - `ID` : The id of the subscriber.
            - `Name` : The name of the subscriber.
            - `Email` : The email of the subscriber.
            - `CreatedOn` : The date time that the subscriber was created.
            - `UpdatedOn` : The date time that the subscriber was updated.
            - `UnsubscribedOn` : The date time that the subscriber was unsubscribed.
            - `UnsubscribedFromID` : The ip that the subscriber was unsubscribed from.
            - `SubscribeType` : The status of the subscriber. It can be one of the following:
                - `1` : Subscribed.
                - `2` : Unsubscribed.
                - `3` : Bounced.
                - `4` : Removed.
            - `CustomFields` :  A list with all the custom fields for the subscriber. This list will contain the following information for each custom field :
                - `CustomFieldID` : The id of the custom field.
                - `Name`: The name of the custom field.
                - `Value` : The value of the custom field.
            - `RemovedOn` : The date time that the subscriber was removed from the list.

    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body 
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": {
                "Paging": {
                  "PageSize": 500,
                  "CurrentPage": 1,
                  "TotalResults": 2,
                  "TotalPageCount": 1,
                  "SortExpression": null,
                  "SortIsAscending": false
                },
                "Subscribers": [
                  {
                    "ID": "07111755-8ee4-1111-ad2b-1111899c6f",
                    "Name": "Paul",
                    "Email": "paul@email.com",
                    "CreatedOn": "/Date(1461777177393+0100)/",
                    "UpdatedOn": "/Date(1461777177393+0100)/",
                    "UnsubscribedOn": null,
                    "UnsubscribedFromID": null,
                    "SubscribeType": 1,
                    "SubscribeMethod": 2,
                    "CustomFields": [
                      {
                        "CustomFieldID": "63705cf2-7cbb-4ac1-a246-1a8c1b416026",
                        "Name": "CheckBox",
                        "Value": "True"
                      },
                      {
                        "CustomFieldID": "63705cf2-7cbb-4ac1-a246-1a8c1b416026",
                        "Name": "Date",
                        "Value": "4/12/2016 12:00:00 AM"
                      },
                      {
                        "CustomFieldID": "9df6dcc4-bef2-47e7-93af-86889b6b6d6a",
                        "Name": "Age",
                        "Value": "25"
                      },
                      {
                        "CustomFieldID": "0d2199aa-65fc-448c-b9fe-199e3b72ebc5",
                        "Name": "Some custom field",
                        "Value": "Something2"
                      },
                      {
                        "CustomFieldID": "46721a6b-09aa-46ff-bab1-a0b75dea24cf",
                        "Name": "Some custom field 2",
                        "Value": "Text2"
                      }
                    ],
                    "RemovedOn": null
                  },
                  {
                    "ID": "0bb00735-7ec7-41de-ab04-d622f67340c4",
                    "Name": "John",
                    "Email": "john@email.com",
                    "CreatedOn": "/Date(1461777334373+0100)/",
                    "UpdatedOn": "/Date(1461783253670+0100)/",
                    "UnsubscribedOn": null,
