## Create & Update Segments [/segments/create.{Format}{?apikey}]

### Creating a new empty segment [POST /lists/{MailingListID}/segments/create.{Format}{?apikey}]
Creates a new empty segment (without criteria) for the given mailing list. You may specify the name of the segment and the way the criteria will match together.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string)
    The ID of the mailing list the specified segment belongs
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.

+ Request 200 (application/json)


    + `Name` : The name of the segment. ***(Required)*** 
    + `MatchType` : Specifies how the segment's criteria will match together. This must be one of the following values. ***(Optional)*** <br/> If not specified, `All` will be assumed.
        * `All` : Only subscribers that match all given criteria will be returned by the segment.
        * `Any` : Subscribers that match any of the given criteria will be returned by the segment.
    + `FetchType` : Specifies how many of the criteria matching subscribers will be contained in the created segment.***(Optional)*** <br/> If not specified, `All` will be assumed.
        *`All` : All criteria matching members will be contained in the created segment.
        *`Top` : Only the maximum number of members defined in `FetchValue` will be contained in the created segment.
        *`TopPercent` : Only the percentage of members defined in `FetchValue` will be contained in the created segment.
    + `FetchValue` : Specifies the maximum number for `FetchType:Top` or percentage for `FetchType:TopPercent`of members to be contained in the created segment.  If not specified, `0` will be assumed.
   
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
        
            {
              "Name":"New Customers",
              "MatchType":"All",
              "FetchType":"Top",
              "FetchValue":"200"
            }
        
+ Response 200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : Contains the id of the new segment.

    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json

    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": 10199
            }
            
### Creating a new segment [POST /lists/{MailingListID}/segments/create.{Format}{?apikey}]
Creates a new segment (with criteria) for the given mailing list. You may specify the name of the segment, the way the criteria will match together and the criteria that you wish to segment your list by.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string)
    The ID of the mailing list the specified segment belongs
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    
    

+ Request 200 (application/json)


    + `Name` : The name of the segment. ***(Required)*** 
    + `MatchType` : Specifies how the segment's criteria will match together. This must be one of the following values. ***(Optional)*** <br/> If not specified, `All` will be assumed.
        * `All` : Only subscribers that match all given criteria will be returned by the segment.
        * `Any` : Subscribers that match any of the given criteria will be returned by the segment.
    + `FetchType` : Specifies how many of the criteria matching subscribers will be contained in the created segment.***(Optional)*** <br/> If not specified, `All` will be assumed.
        *`All` : All criteria matching members will be contained in the created segment.
        *`Top` : Only the maximum number of members defined in `FetchValue` will be contained in the created segment.
        *`TopPercent` : Only the percentage of members defined in `FetchValue` will be contained in the created segment.
    + `FetchValue` : Specifies the maximum number for `FetchType:Top` or percentage for `FetchType:TopPercent`of members to be contained in the created segment.  If not specified, `0` will be assumed.
    + `Criteria` : An array of the criteria to filter the mailing list by.
        + `Field` : The field of the criterion to filter the mailing list by. This must be one of the following values. ***(Required)***
            * `DateAdded` : Filters subscribers by the date they were added to the mailing list.  *(Data Type: Date  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, IsBefore, IsAfter, IsBetween, IsNotBetween">?</abbr>)*
            * `DateUpdated` : Filters subscribers by the date they were last updated. *(Data Type: Date  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, IsBefore, IsAfter, IsBetween, IsNotBetween">?</abbr>)*
            * `RecipientName` : Filters subscribers by the recipient name.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith, IsEmpty, IsNotEmpty">?</abbr>)*
            * `RecipientEmail` : Filters subscribers by their email address. *(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
            *  `SubscribeMethod` : Filters subscribers according to their subscribe method.*(Data Type: Enum  <abbr title="SubscriptionForm = 0, FileImport = 1, ManuallyAdded = 2 / Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot">?</abbr>)*
            * `CustomField` : Filters subscribers according to a Custom Field's value.*(Data Type: String, Decimal, DateTime, Boolean  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators vary, depending on Custom Field Type.">?</abbr>)*
            * `MailingList` : Filters subscribers according whether they belong to a specific Mailing List.*(Data Type: GUID  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot">?</abbr>)*
            * `CampaignsOpened` : Filters subscribers according to how many campaigns they have opened (within the past 60 days maximum). *(Data Type: Integer  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, IsGreaterThan, IsGreaterThanOrEqualTo, IsLessThan, IsLessThanOrEqualTo, IsBetween, IsNotBetween">?</abbr>)*
            * `LinksClicked` : Filters subscribers according to how many links they have clicked from previous campaigns sent to them (within the past 60 days maximum).*(Data Type: Integer  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, IsGreaterThan, IsGreaterThanOrEqualTo, IsLessThan, IsLessThanOrEqualTo, IsBetween, IsNotBetween">?</abbr>)*
            * `CampaignName` : Filters subscribers according to which campaigns they have opened, based on their names.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
            * `LinkURL` : Filters subscribers according to which links they have clicked, based on their urls.*(Data Type: Guid  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot">?</abbr>)*
            * `CampaignSent` : Filters subscribers according to the campaign that they received or did not receive. *(Data Type: Guid  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot">?</abbr>)*
            * `Platform` : Filters subscribers according to which platform use. *(Data Type: Enum  <abbr title="Desktop = 1, Mobile = 2, Other = 3 / Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot">?</abbr>)*
            * `OperatingSystems` : Filters subscribers according to their operating system.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
            * `EmailClient` : Filters subscribers according to their email client.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
            * `WebBrowser` : Filters subscribers according to their web browser.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
            * `MobileBrowser` : Filters subscribers according to their mobile browser.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
            * `AddedAnythingToCart` : Filters subscribers according to their Tracked Website's Cart history. *(Data Type: Boolean  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : IsTrue, IsFalse">?</abbr>)*
            * `ViewedProduct` : Filters subscribers according to their Tracked Website's Browsing history. *(Data Type: Boolean  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : IsTrue, IsFalse">?</abbr>)*
            * `PurchasedProduct` : Filters subscribers according to their Tracked Website's Purchase history. *(Data Type: Boolean  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : IsTrue, IsFalse">?</abbr>)*
    
    
        + `Comparer` : An operator that defines the way to compare a criterion field with its value. This must be one of the following values. ***(Optional)*** <br/> If not specified, `Is` will be assumed.
            * `Is` : To find subscribers where the field is exactly equal to the search term.
            * `IsNot` : To find subscribers where the field is other than the search term.
            * `Contains` : To find subscribers where the field contains the search term.
            * `DoesNotContain` : To find subscribers where the field does not contain the search term.
            * `StartsWith` : To find subscribers where the field starts with the search term.
            * `DoesNotStartWith` : To find subscribers where the field does not start with the search term.
            * `EndsWith` : To find subscribers where the field ends with the search term.
            * `DoesNotEndWith`: To find subscribers where the field does not end with the search term.
            * `IsGreaterThan` : To find subscribers where the field is greater than the search term.
            * `IsGreaterThanOrEqualTo` : To find subscribers where the field is greater than or equal to the search term.
            * `IsLessThan` : To find subscribers where the field is less than the search term.
            * `IsLessThanOrEqualTo` : To find subscribers where the field is less than or equal to the search term.
            * `IsBefore` : To find subscribers where the specified date field is before the specified date value.
            * `IsAfter` : To find subscribers where the specified date field is after the specified date value.
            * `IsEmpty` : To find subscribers where the field contains no value. *(<abbr title=" IsEmpty and IsNotEmpty are available when the field is nullable">?</abbr>)*
            * `IsNotEmpty` : To find subscribers excluding those where the field contains no value.*(<abbr title=" IsEmpty and IsNotEmpty are available when the field is nullable">?</abbr>)*
            * `IsTrue`: To find subscribers where the condition defined by the field is true.
            * `IsFalse`: To find subscribers where the condition defined by the field is false.
    
        + `Value` : A search term to filter the specified field by. ***(Optional)***
        + `LastXMinutes` parameter constrains the results in relevance to the time that has elapsed
        +`DateFrom` and `DateTo` parameters constrain the results based on a specific date span
    
        + `Date Functions`: Can be used with fields of DateTime data type. 
            * `Year`:The year part of the date *(4 digits)*
            * `Month`: The month part of the date *(1-12)*
            * `Day`: The day part of the date *(1-31)*
            * `WeekDay`: The week day of the date *(1-7, Sunday = 1, Monday = 2, etc)*
            * `DaysPassed`: Number of days that have passed until now
            * `HoursPassed`: Number of hours that have passed until now
            * `MinutesPassed`: Number of minutes that have passed until now


   
         
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
        
            {
              "Name":"Engaged and Verified",
              "MatchType":"All",
              "FetchType":"All",
              "Criteria": [
                  {
                    "Field":"VerifiedForDoubleOptIn",
                    "Comparer":"IsTrue"
                  },
                  {
                    "Field":"LinksClicked",
                    "Comparer":"Is",
                    "Value":"2",
                    "LastXMinutes":43200
                  }
                ]
            }
        
+ Response 200 (application/json)


    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : Contains the id of the new segment.

    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json

    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": 10199
            }
### Updating a segment [POST /lists/{MailingListID}/segments/{SegmentID}/update.{Format}{?apikey}]
Updates the properties and criteria of an existing segment. You may update the name and match type of the segment. If criteria are included these will also be updated. You may update only the criteria. In that case, the existing name and settings will be retained.

+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string)
    The ID of the mailing list the specified segment belongs
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.

+ Request 200 (application/json)


    + `Name` : The name of the segment. ***(Optional)*** <br/> If not specified, the existing name will be retained.
    + `MatchType` : Specifies how the segment's criteria will match together. This must be one of the following values. ***(Optional)*** <br/> If not specified, existing settings will be retained.
        * `All` : Only subscribers that match all given criteria will be returned by the segment.
        * `Any` : Subscribers that match any of the given criteria will be returned by the segment.
    + `FetchType` : Specifies how many of the criteria matching subscribers will be contained in the created segment. ***(Optional)*** <br/> If not specified, existing settings will be retained.
        *`All` : All criteria matching members will be contained in the created segment.
        *`Top` : Only the maximum number of members defined in `FetchValue` will be contained in the created segment.
        *`TopPercent` : Only the percentage of members defined in `FetchValue` will be contained in the created segment.
    + `FetchValue` : Specifies the maximum number for `FetchType:Top` or percentage for `FetchType:TopPercent`of members to be contained in the created segment.  If not specified, `0` will be assumed.
    + `Criteria` : An array of the criteria to filter the mailing list by. ***(Optional)*** <br/> If not specified, existing criteria will be retained.
        + `Field` : The field of the criterion to filter the mailing list by. This must be one of the following values. ***(Required)***
            * `DateAdded` : Filters subscribers by the date they were added to the mailing list.  *(Data Type: Date  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, IsBefore, IsAfter, IsBetween, IsNotBetween">?</abbr>)*
            * `DateUpdated` : Filters subscribers by the date they were last updated. *(Data Type: Date  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, IsBefore, IsAfter, IsBetween, IsNotBetween">?</abbr>)*
            * `RecipientName` : Filters subscribers by the recipient name.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith, IsEmpty, IsNotEmpty">?</abbr>)*
            * `RecipientEmail` : Filters subscribers by their email address. *(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
            *  `SubscribeMethod` : Filters subscribers according to their subscribe method.*(Data Type: Enum  <abbr title="SubscriptionForm = 0, FileImport = 1, ManuallyAdded = 2 / Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot">?</abbr>)*
            * `CustomField` : Filters subscribers according to a Custom Field's value.*(Data Type: String, Decimal, DateTime, Boolean  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators vary, depending on Custom Field Type.">?</abbr>)*
            * `MailingList` : Filters subscribers according whether they belong to a specific Mailing List.*(Data Type: GUID  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot">?</abbr>)*
            * `CampaignsOpened` : Filters subscribers according to how many campaigns they have opened (within the past 60 days maximum). *(Data Type: Integer  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, IsGreaterThan, IsGreaterThanOrEqualTo, IsLessThan, IsLessThanOrEqualTo, IsBetween, IsNotBetween">?</abbr>)*
            * `LinksClicked` : Filters subscribers according to how many links they have clicked from previous campaigns sent to them (within the past 60 days maximum).*(Data Type: Integer  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, IsGreaterThan, IsGreaterThanOrEqualTo, IsLessThan, IsLessThanOrEqualTo, IsBetween, IsNotBetween">?</abbr>)*
            * `CampaignName` : Filters subscribers according to which campaigns they have opened, based on their names.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
            * `LinkURL` : Filters subscribers according to which links they have clicked, based on their urls.*(Data Type: Guid  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot">?</abbr>)*
            * `CampaignSent` : Filters subscribers according to the campaign that they received or did not receive. *(Data Type: Guid  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot">?</abbr>)*
            * `Platform` : Filters subscribers according to which platform use. *(Data Type: Enum  <abbr title="Desktop = 1, Mobile = 2, Other = 3 / Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot">?</abbr>)*
            * `OperatingSystems` : Filters subscribers according to their operating system.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
            * `EmailClient` : Filters subscribers according to their email client.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
            * `WebBrowser` : Filters subscribers according to their web browser.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
            * `MobileBrowser` : Filters subscribers according to their mobile browser.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
            * `AddedAnythingToCart` : Filters subscribers according to their Tracked Website's Cart history. *(Data Type: Boolean  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : IsTrue, IsFalse">?</abbr>)*
            * `ViewedProduct` : Filters subscribers according to their Tracked Website's Browsing history. *(Data Type: Boolean  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : IsTrue, IsFalse">?</abbr>)*
            * `PurchasedProduct` : Filters subscribers according to their Tracked Website's Purchase history. *(Data Type: Boolean  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : IsTrue, IsFalse">?</abbr>)*
    
    
        + `Comparer` : An operator that defines the way to compare a criterion field with its value. This must be one of the following values. ***(Optional)*** <br/> If not specified, `Is` will be assumed.
            * `Is` : To find subscribers where the field is exactly equal to the search term.
            * `IsNot` : To find subscribers where the field is other than the search term.
            * `Contains` : To find subscribers where the field contains the search term.
            * `DoesNotContain` : To find subscribers where the field does not contain the search term.
            * `StartsWith` : To find subscribers where the field starts with the search term.
            * `DoesNotStartWith` : To find subscribers where the field does not start with the search term.
            * `EndsWith` : To find subscribers where the field ends with the search term.
            * `DoesNotEndWith`: To find subscribers where the field does not end with the search term.
            * `IsGreaterThan` : To find subscribers where the field is greater than the search term.
            * `IsGreaterThanOrEqualTo` : To find subscribers where the field is greater than or equal to the search term.
            * `IsLessThan` : To find subscribers where the field is less than the search term.
            * `IsLessThanOrEqualTo` : To find subscribers where the field is less than or equal to the search term.
            * `IsBefore` : To find subscribers where the specified date field is before the specified date value.
            * `IsAfter` : To find subscribers where the specified date field is after the specified date value.
            * `IsEmpty` : To find subscribers where the field contains no value. *(<abbr title=" IsEmpty and IsNotEmpty are available when the field is nullable">?</abbr>)*
            * `IsNotEmpty` : To find subscribers excluding those where the field contains no value.*(<abbr title=" IsEmpty and IsNotEmpty are available when the field is nullable">?</abbr>)*
            * `IsTrue`: To find subscribers where the condition defined by the field is true.
            * `IsFalse`: To find subscribers where the condition defined by the field is false.
    
        + `Value` : A search term to filter the specified field by. ***(Optional)***
        + `LastXMinutes` parameter constrains the results in relevance to the time that has elapsed
        +`DateFrom` and `DateTo` parameters constrain the results based on a specific date span
    
        + `Date Functions`: Can be used with fields of DateTime data type. 
            * `Year`:The year part of the date *(4 digits)*
            * `Month`: The month part of the date *(1-12)*
            * `Day`: The day part of the date *(1-31)*
            * `WeekDay`: The week day of the date *(1-7, Sunday = 1, Monday = 2, etc)*
            * `DaysPassed`: Number of days that have passed until now
            * `HoursPassed`: Number of hours that have passed until now
            * `MinutesPassed`: Number of minutes that have passed until now

         
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
        
            {
              "Name":"Customer Tracking and Opener",
              "MatchType":"Any",
              "FetchType":"All",
              "Criteria": [
                  {
                    "Field":"AddedAnythingToCart",
                    "Comparer":"IsTrue",
                    "Times":2,
                    "ProductCode":"123",
                    "LastXMinutes":4320,
                    "WebsiteId":"12345678-1234-abdc-efgh-1231bc456efg789hij"
                  },
                  {
                    "Field":"OpenedAnyCampaign",
                    "Comparer":"IsTrue",
                    "DateFrom":"2019-09-01",
                    "DateTo":"2020-12-01"
                  }
                ]
            }
        
+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response message. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : The response context for this call. This will be null if successful.

    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json

    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": null
            }

### Adding criteria to segments[POST /lists/{MailingListID}/segments/{SegmentID}/criteria/add.{Format}{?apikey}]
Adds a new criterion (a rule) to the specified segment.


+ Parameters
    + Format: json (required, string)
    
         + Members
            + json
            + xml
            
    + MailingListID: `a589366a-1a34-4965-ac50-f1299fe5979e` (required, string)
    The ID of the mailing list the specified segment belongs.
    + apikey: `13cffeee-0b8c-4610-8e0d-efa7bd44be32` (required, string)
    You may find your API Key or generate a new one in your account settings.
    + SegmentID: 10199 (required, string)
    The ID of the segment to update.

        
+ Request 200 (application/json)


  + `Field` : The field of the criterion to filter the mailing list by. This must be one of the following values. ***(Required)***
        * `DateAdded` : Filters subscribers by the date they were added to the mailing list.  *(Data Type: Date  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, IsBefore, IsAfter, IsBetween, IsNotBetween">?</abbr>)*
        * `DateUpdated` : Filters subscribers by the date they were last updated. *(Data Type: Date  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, IsBefore, IsAfter, IsBetween, IsNotBetween">?</abbr>)*
        * `RecipientName` : Filters subscribers by the recipient name.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith, IsEmpty, IsNotEmpty">?</abbr>)*
        * `RecipientEmail` : Filters subscribers by their email address. *(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
        *  `SubscribeMethod` : Filters subscribers according to their subscribe method.*(Data Type: Enum  <abbr title="SubscriptionForm = 0, FileImport = 1, ManuallyAdded = 2 / Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot">?</abbr>)*
        * `CustomField` : Filters subscribers according to a Custom Field's value.*(Data Type: String, Decimal, DateTime, Boolean  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators vary, depending on Custom Field Type.">?</abbr>)*
        * `MailingList` : Filters subscribers according whether they belong to a specific Mailing List.*(Data Type: GUID  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot">?</abbr>)*
        * `CampaignsOpened` : Filters subscribers according to how many campaigns they have opened (within the past 60 days maximum). *(Data Type: Integer  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, IsGreaterThan, IsGreaterThanOrEqualTo, IsLessThan, IsLessThanOrEqualTo, IsBetween, IsNotBetween">?</abbr>)*
        * `LinksClicked` : Filters subscribers according to how many links they have clicked from previous campaigns sent to them (within the past 60 days maximum).*(Data Type: Integer  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, IsGreaterThan, IsGreaterThanOrEqualTo, IsLessThan, IsLessThanOrEqualTo, IsBetween, IsNotBetween">?</abbr>)*
        * `CampaignName` : Filters subscribers according to which campaigns they have opened, based on their names.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
        * `LinkURL` : Filters subscribers according to which links they have clicked, based on their urls.*(Data Type: Guid  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot">?</abbr>)*
        * `CampaignSent` : Filters subscribers according to the campaign that they received or did not receive. *(Data Type: Guid  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot">?</abbr>)*
        * `Platform` : Filters subscribers according to which platform use. *(Data Type: Enum  <abbr title="Desktop = 1, Mobile = 2, Other = 3 / Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot">?</abbr>)*
        * `OperatingSystems` : Filters subscribers according to their operating system.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
        * `EmailClient` : Filters subscribers according to their email client.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
        * `WebBrowser` : Filters subscribers according to their web browser.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
        * `MobileBrowser` : Filters subscribers according to their mobile browser.*(Data Type: String  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : Is, IsNot, Contains, DoesNotContain, StartsWith, DoesNotStartWith, EndsWith, DoesNotEndWith">?</abbr>)*
        * `AddedAnythingToCart` : Filters subscribers according to their Tracked Website's Cart history. *(Data Type: Boolean  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : IsTrue, IsFalse">?</abbr>)*
        * `ViewedProduct` : Filters subscribers according to their Tracked Website's Browsing history. *(Data Type: Boolean  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : IsTrue, IsFalse">?</abbr>)*
        * `PurchasedProduct` : Filters subscribers according to their Tracked Website's Purchase history. *(Data Type: Boolean  <abbr title="Compatible Query Operators : IsTrue, IsFalse">?</abbr>)*


    + `Comparer` : An operator that defines the way to compare a criterion field with its value. This must be one of the following values. ***(Optional)*** <br/> If not specified, `Is` will be assumed.
        * `Is` : To find subscribers where the field is exactly equal to the search term.
        * `IsNot` : To find subscribers where the field is other than the search term.
        * `Contains` : To find subscribers where the field contains the search term.
        * `DoesNotContain` : To find subscribers where the field does not contain the search term.
        * `StartsWith` : To find subscribers where the field starts with the search term.
        * `DoesNotStartWith` : To find subscribers where the field does not start with the search term.
        * `EndsWith` : To find subscribers where the field ends with the search term.
        * `DoesNotEndWith`: To find subscribers where the field does not end with the search term.
        * `IsGreaterThan` : To find subscribers where the field is greater than the search term.
        * `IsGreaterThanOrEqualTo` : To find subscribers where the field is greater than or equal to the search term.
        * `IsLessThan` : To find subscribers where the field is less than the search term.
        * `IsLessThanOrEqualTo` : To find subscribers where the field is less than or equal to the search term.
        * `IsBefore` : To find subscribers where the specified date field is before the specified date value.
        * `IsAfter` : To find subscribers where the specified date field is after the specified date value.
        * `IsEmpty` : To find subscribers where the field contains no value. *(<abbr title=" IsEmpty and IsNotEmpty are available when the field is nullable">?</abbr>)*
        * `IsNotEmpty` : To find subscribers excluding those where the field contains no value.*(<abbr title=" IsEmpty and IsNotEmpty are available when the field is nullable">?</abbr>)*
        * `IsTrue`: To find subscribers where the condition defined by the field is true.
        * `IsFalse`: To find subscribers where the condition defined by the field is false.

    + `Value` : A search term to filter the specified field by. ***(Optional)***
    + `LastXMinutes` parameter constrains the results in relevance to the time that has elapsed
    +`DateFrom` and `DateTo` parameters constrain the results based on a specific date span

    + `Date Functions`: Can be used with fields of DateTime data type. 
        * `Year`:The year part of the date *(4 digits)*
        * `Month`: The month part of the date *(1-12)*
        * `Day`: The day part of the date *(1-31)*
        * `WeekDay`: The week day of the date *(1-7, Sunday = 1, Monday = 2, etc)*
        * `DaysPassed`: Number of days that have passed until now
        * `HoursPassed`: Number of hours that have passed until now
        * `MinutesPassed`: Number of minutes that have passed until now


   
         
    
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
    
    + Body
    
            {
                "Field":"DateAdded",
                "DateFunction": "Year",
                "Comparer":"Is","Value":"2020"
            }

        
+ Response 200 (application/json)

    
    + `Code` : The response code for this call. This will be 0 if successful.
    + `Error` : The response error for this call. This will be null if successful.
    + `Context` : Contains the new criteriaID.

   
    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
            
    + Body
    
            {
              "Code": 0,
              "Error": null,
              "Context": 15783
            }

